  <metadata>
    <name>Alpine MTB Map</name>
    <desc>Lift-served mountain-bike spots in the western Alps and Jura. Trail geometries from OpenStreetMap (ODbL).</desc>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="43.656719" lon="40.268184">
    <name>Krasnaya Polyana Bike Park (Sochi, Russia)</name>
    <desc>Vodopad Polikarya chairlift 1375 m - top of the lift serving the upper bike-park trails

    Trails
About 30 km of purpose-built gravity trails between roughly 1,375 m and 540 m, graded green, blue, red and black. The network mixes long flow sections with berms and rhythm features, steep technical lines, drops, wooden features, a skills park and pump track. The lower K1 gondola carries bikes between Polyana 540 and Polyana 960; the Vodopad Polikarya chairlift serves the upper sector.

    Getting up / price
Bike-pass required from 09:00 to 17:00 and sold at Polyana 540 and 960. Bikes use the external racks on the Krasnaya Polyana K1 gondola and the designated carriers on the Vodopad Polikarya chairlift. Check the live lift and trail status and current tariff before travelling.

    Open season
Open from 01 May; closed from 01 November (typical summer operating window; snow and maintenance can shorten the upper sector season).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
The resort lies within Sochi National Park; access above 960 m may require a separate national-park permit.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Sochi / Adler airport | Car / taxi | 50-70 min
Esto-Sadok | Bus / taxi | 10 min

    Sources: official live bike-park and lift status, official trail overview and official bike-park rules. Lift-top coordinate cross-checked against the published Vodopad Polikarya upper-station coordinate.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="43.564720" lon="41.189370">
    <name>Arkhyz Bike Park (Russia)</name>
    <desc>Mlechny Put gondola 2240 m - top station on the south side

    Trails
More than 30 km of prepared bike-park trails across the south and north sectors. Green progression trails occupy the south slope, with blue and red flow and jump trails plus black expert lines and rougher northern-slope riding. Descents start in alpine terrain and continue through conifer forest; the park also hosts downhill, enduro, dual-slalom and e-MTB events.

    Getting up / price
The Mlechny Put gondola serves the south side and carries bikes in marked cabins. The 2026 one-day bike pass is 3,350 RUB adult / 2,450 RUB child; multi-day and season passes are available. Rental, workshop, instruction and guiding are available at the resort.

    Open season
Open from 16 May; closed from 16 October (published 2026 period).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:30
The north sector may open later because of snow. Lift maintenance days and weather closures occur; check the official status before travelling.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Mineralnye Vody airport | Car / shuttle | 3-3.5 h
Arkhyz village | Car / taxi | 15-20 min

    Sources: official bike-park site, published 2026 season and hours, official 2026 prices and trail information and the resort's published GPS coordinate for the Mlechny Put upper station.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="55.949087" lon="92.786265">
    <name>Bobrovy Log Bike Park (Krasnoyarsk, Russia)</name>
    <desc>K1 chairlift 514 m - top station above Krasnoyarsk

    Trails
Compact lift-served gravity riding on the steep, forested edge of the Eastern Sayan. The official bike park includes a skills zone and prepared downhill trails; DH trail 8 is the main advanced line, with fast berms, technical forest sections and race features. Blue and red training trails are used by the local MTB academy, and the park regularly hosts Fun Bike Race downhill events.

    Getting up / price
The K1 detachable chairlift carries mountain bikes on designated chairs. The published 2026 bike pass costs 1,000 RUB for four hours or 1,350 RUB for the day. Operation is conditional on trail inspection, weather and the K1 schedule.

    Open season
Open from 01 June; closed from 01 October (typical snow-free operating window; check the official schedule).
Daily opening hours: according to K1 lift schedule
DH trail 8 opens only after inspection. A suitable mountain bike, helmet and protective equipment are required.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Central Krasnoyarsk | Car / taxi / bus | 15-30 min
Krasnoyarsk airport | Car / taxi | 50-70 min

    Sources: official bike-park information and 2026 prices, official bike-park rules and OSM K1 upper station node 1503587400 (ODbL).</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.791035" lon="85.830386">
    <name>Manzherok Bike Park (Altai, Russia)</name>
    <desc>Vostok chairlift 1240 m - upper station on Malaya Sinyukha

    Trails
Lift-served downhill and enduro terrain on Malaya Sinyukha above Lake Manzherok. Published descriptions list green, blue, red and black gravity trails with berms, drops, steep turns and wooden skills features. The resort has expanded substantially, so published totals vary from about 7 km for the original downhill park to roughly 13 km for the wider bike-park network.

    Getting up / price
The Vostok chairlift reaches the 1,240 m upper station and connects to descending trails including mapped routes Argut, Maral and Velvet. Bike transport and the applicable downhill tariff should be confirmed with the resort before travelling; the older published bike-park information refers to a dedicated bike pass.

    Open season
Open from 01 June; closed from 01 October (typical summer window; current MTB operating dates not published clearly online).
Daily opening hours: check with resort
Manzherok has undergone major lift and trail redevelopment. Confirm which gravity trails and bike-carrying lifts are open before travel.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Gorno-Altaysk airport | Car / taxi | 30-40 min
Manzherok village | Car / taxi | 10-15 min

    Sources: published Manzherok bike-park overview and OSM Vostok upper station node 9729515306 (ODbL), mapped at 1,240 m and operated by Manzherok.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="37.490917" lon="71.548922">
    <name>Khorog - Pamir Highway and Wakhan (Tajikistan) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Remote high-altitude mountain-bike expeditions through the Pamirs

    Trails
Khorog is the main riding and logistics base for the Pamir Highway, Wakhan Valley and Gorno-Badakhshan. This is expedition terrain rather than a trail centre: long gravel stages cross passes above 4,000 m, with rough descents including Koi-Tezek, Nayzatash and Ak-Baital. Side valleys add unmaintained tracks, river crossings and very isolated mountain riding.

    Getting up / price
No lift. Most trips combine pedalling with a 4x4 support vehicle, luggage transport and local guiding. Independent riding is possible for experienced expedition cyclists, but distances, altitude and limited supplies make supported travel strongly advisable.

    Open season
Open from 01 July; closed from 01 October (average high-pass riding window).
Daily opening hours: daylight hours
A GBAO permit is required. Some border areas and Zorkul require additional permission; rules, crossings and road conditions can change at short notice.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Khorog | Bike / 4x4 | Direct
Dushanbe | Flight / long 4x4 transfer | Variable

    Sources: Travel to Tajikistan sports tourism, the Pamir Guides bike-tour itinerary and Travel Tajikistan Pamir Highway itinerary. Confirm permits, security advice and current road access before departure.</desc>
  </wpt>
