  <wpt lat="41.559475" lon="70.015402">
    <name>Chimgan - Ugam-Chatkal (Uzbekistan) [no bike lift documented]</name>
    <desc>Natural Tian Shan enduro and adventure riding above Charvak Reservoir

    Trails
Chimgan is the main mountain base near Tashkent, with rocky jeep tracks, shepherd paths, gorge descents and steep natural terrain in the Ugam-Chatkal mountains. It is best approached as a guided backcountry ride rather than a maintained bike park; trail marking and reliable difficulty information are limited.

    Getting up / price
Pedal access or locally arranged vehicle support. No operating mountain-bike lift is documented. Nearby Amirsoy runs gondolas for sightseeing, but its official summer activity information does not confirm bicycle carriage.

    Open season
Open from 01 May; closed from 01 November (average snow-free riding season).
Daily opening hours: daylight hours
Confirm the route, protected-area rules and any permit requirements with a local guide before riding.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Tashkent | Car | ~1 h 30
Chimgan village | Bike | Direct

    Sources: Amirsoy official activities and Visit Tashkent mountain-area information. Current MTB infrastructure is not formally documented, so verify locally.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="42.599493" lon="78.500159">
    <name>Jyrgalan Valley MTB (Kyrgyzstan) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Community-based natural mountain biking in the eastern Tian Shan

    Trails
Marked village routes include the 7 km Tulpar Tash ride, the 13 km Kok-Bel waterfall route and the 16.6 km Eki Chat loop. Stronger riders can tackle the rough Kok-Bel Pass route, with alpine terrain, river valleys and technical natural sections. Local guesthouses arrange rentals and guides.

    Getting up / price
Pedal access; no lift. Guided rides and vehicle support can be arranged locally. The destination lists bike rental at 1,320 KGS per day or 660 KGS per half day; confirm current rates.

    Open season
Open from 01 June; closed from 01 October (official recommended riding season is June to September).
Daily opening hours: daylight hours
Mountain weather changes quickly. Carry repair and navigation equipment, and use a local guide for remote routes.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Karakol | Car | ~1 h
Jyrgalan village | Bike | Direct

    Source: Destination Jyrgalan official mountain-biking guide. Check current trail and rental conditions locally.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="42.481740" lon="78.400293">
    <name>Karakol - Jeti-Oguz MTB (Kyrgyzstan) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Natural Tian Shan enduro and multi-day riding hub

    Trails
Karakol is the principal base for forest singletrack, alpine valleys and long natural descents around Jeti-Oguz and the eastern Issyk-Kul region. Riding ranges from approachable valley routes to remote high-pass adventures with substantial climbing and exposed mountain terrain.

    Getting up / price
Pedal access or a locally arranged shuttle; no lift-served bike park is documented. Do not assume that nearby ski lifts carry bicycles. Karakol has bike rental and guiding operators for day rides and supported multi-day trips.

    Open season
Open from 01 June; closed from 15 October (average high-country riding season).
Daily opening hours: daylight hours
Route conditions and river crossings vary. A guide is strongly recommended outside the lower valley network.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Karakol | Bike / car | Direct
Bishkek | Car | ~5 h

    Source: Visit Kyrgyzstan Karakol mountain-biking guide. Confirm routes, guides and access before departure.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.518879" lon="6.275959">
    <name>Saint-George / Mont Chaubert [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Mont Chaubert - pedal-up Jura vaudois riding

    Trails
Four marked natural descents near Saint-George: Mont Chaubert, Mont Bailly, its eastern variant and La Plagne. Short, rooty and rocky Jura singletrack with no mechanical uplift; climb from Saint-George or arrange a local shuttle. The routes are shared forest paths, so follow local MTB signs and give way to other users.

    Getting up / price
No bike lift. Pedal up from Saint-George or use a local shuttle. Free access where permitted.

    Open season
Open from 01 April; closed from 01 December (typical window; check local conditions and forestry notices).

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Saint-George | Bike / car | Local access
Lausanne | Train + bike | ~1h15

    Sources: Parc Jura vaudois MTB information, Saint-George MTB routes and the individual OpenStreetMap links on each trace. Verify access, trail status and local rules before riding.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.454526" lon="6.111707">
    <name>St-Cergue / La Dôle (Jura vaudois) [train fare only]</name>
    <desc>La Givrine (top of the NStCM train)

    Trails
The closest real singletrack riding to Lausanne. Three marked descents drop off the Jura crest back towards Arzier and St-Cergue: Mont Chaubert, Mont Bailly (plus an eastern variant) and La Plagne. Rooty, rocky, north-facing forest trails, short (1-2 km each) but you can chain them and pedal back up in 20-30 min, or reload with the train. Dry quickly, ridable from April to November - the best shoulder-season option on this map.

Rain sensitivity
Rain-resilient: rocky Jura ground drains quickly despite the shaded forest; heavy same-day rain can still make roots slick.

    Getting up / price
No lift needed: the train is the climb (Nyon 400 m &gt; La Givrine 1228 m). Normal CFF/NStCM fare, plus a bike ticket - the national day bike pass is about 14 CHF (bikes are carried on the NStCM, space is limited at peak times).

    Open season
Open from 1 April; closed from 1 December (typical window; check the operator and conditions).

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train | ~1h05

    Source: NStCM railway.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
