  <wpt lat="46.334342" lon="7.479508">
    <name>Crans-Montana - Cry d'Er [35 CHF]</name>
    <desc>Cry d'Er 2263 m - top of the Crans gondola

    Trails
Three downhill runs covering every level plus a new flowtrail. Flowtrail Arnouva is the beginner line - wide, rolling, a good place to learn to let go of the brakes. Cry d'Er Downhill is the intermediate/technical one: berms, rock features and a proper rhythm section. Beyond the park, Freeride Grand Montana and the Montana-Village &gt; Loc flowtrail give you long natural descents through the larch forest all the way to the valley.

    Getting up / price
Summer day pass around 35 CHF; Crans - Cry d'Er return alone is 25 CHF. Bike park runs 13 June - 25 October 2026.

    Open season
Open from 13 June; closed from 26 October (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train + funicular | ~1h30

    Source: Crans-Montana bike.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.

    Rain sensitivity
Rain-resilient: sunny, high-altitude larch-forest and open terrain that drains well - only heavy rain on the day itself makes it properly wet.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.320660" lon="7.498832">
    <name>Crans-Montana: Les Violettes / Les Barzettes</name>
    <desc>Second lift access on the Montana side, useful for reaching the Plaine Morte end of the domain and the longer natural descents back to the valley.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <trk>
    <name>Crans-Montana: Plaine Morte - Sion epic</name>
    <desc>~26 km high-alpine ridge descent from the Plaine Morte glacier (2880 m) to Sion, dropping ~2400 m past Col du Rawyl, Schnidejoch and Sex Rouge. Long, remote terrain: check conditions before riding. Source: recorded.</desc>
