  <wpt lat="46.555639" lon="7.023757">
    <name>Moléson-sur-Gruyères [38 CHF / Magic Pass]</name>
    <desc>Plan-Francey 1520 m - bike park base

    Trails
Bike Park Moleson, based at Plan-Francey and served by the funicular then the chairlift. Modzon and Poya are the flowy, accessible runs - genuinely good for progressing riders. Tche Don is the technical enduro line, steeper and rougher. Small park, but well built, rarely crowded, and the Gruyeres backdrop is hard to beat.

    Getting up / price
Journee bike (funicular + cable car + chairlift) 38 CHF; a 4-hour bike ticket (funicular + chairlift) is 29 CHF. Free with the Magic Pass.

    Open season
Open from 15 May; closed from 2 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train + bus | ~1h40

    Source: Moleson.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.547247" lon="7.018134">
    <name>Moleson: Le Moléson 2002 m - summit cable car station</name>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.321886" lon="7.073167">
    <name>Villars-Gryon - Col de Bretaye [36 CHF / Magic Pass]</name>
    <desc>Col de Bretaye 1806 m - top of the Villars cog railway

    Trails
The Grand Chamossaire descent, opened in summer 2025: 3 km of blue flow with big berms, a few technical sections and smooth fast bits between them - built for families and improving riders rather than for hucking. Around it sits a dense network of marked SuisseMobile routes: 573 Bretaye &gt; Villars, 572 Bretaye &gt; Ollon (a long 20 km+ descent to the Rhone valley), 580 towards Les Chaux and Solalex, and 582 Taveyanne-Solalex. Villars also preserves the Maxi Avalanche line toward the valley, with roughly 1500 m of vertical from the Roc d'Orsay sector.

    Getting up / price
TVGD summer day pass 36 CHF adult / 18 CHF child, covering the Villars-Bretaye train, the gondolas and the Grand Chamossaire chairlift. Single ascent 20 CHF. Free with the Magic Pass. Mid-June to late October.

    Open season
Open from 15 June; closed from 26 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train | ~1h45

    Sources: Villars-Diablerets and the official Grand Chamossaire and Maxi Avalanche overview.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.326579" lon="7.061778">
    <name>Bretaye: Grand Chamossaire 2120 m - top of the chairlift</name>
  </wpt>
