  <wpt lat="46.333290" lon="7.121228">
    <name>Les Diablerets [36 CHF / Magic Pass]</name>
    <desc>Meilleret 1949 m - top of the chairlift

    Trails
Isenau Bike (SuisseMobile route 590) is the classic: an 8 km climb out of the village, then a descent split between a vehicle-width track and a forest path that asks for some skill. If you do not fancy the technical part, the tarmac road back to Les Diablerets is right there. Stage 2 of the Alpes du Leman Bike route continues from here down to Bex.

    Getting up / price
Same TVGD day pass as Villars, 36 CHF, free with the Magic Pass. Important caveat: the old Isenau gondola was dismantled and has not been replaced, so the Meilleret chairlift is the summer lift here - check it is actually turning before you commit.

    Open season
Open from 1 July; closed from 1 September (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train | ~1h25

    Source: Villars-Diablerets.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
