  <wpt lat="46.314928" lon="7.385609">
    <name>Anzère - Pas de Maimbré [bikes ride free]</name>
    <desc>Pas-de-Maimbré 2362 m - top of the Anzère gondola

    Trails
Phoenix Ride is a 1.5 km red downhill trail with about 380 m of descent from La Dent, reached from the gondola mid-station. Five official enduro routes add options from the easy, lift-assisted Gentiane Bike Light to the longer intermediate Arnica and Tulipe loops. High, open and dry: a good choice in a wet spell lower down.

    Getting up / price
Carrying a mountain bike on the gondola is free in summer, which makes this unusually good value; you only pay your own passenger ticket. Anzere is a Magic Pass resort.

    Open season
Open from 15 June; closed from 19 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train + bus | ~1h50

    Source: Anzere tourism.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <trk>
    <name>Anzere: Arnica Bike</name>
    <desc>17.6 km intermediate enduro loop, +733/-733 m. From Anzere it climbs through the Grillesses mayens, follows the Bisse de Sion towards Les Rousses and Pra Combere, then returns through the Serin, Duez and Tsalan alpine pastures before descending via La Brune. Source: Anzere Tourism. Official GPX geometry supplied by Anzere Tourism, simplified to 15 m.</desc>
