  <wpt lat="46.766233" lon="9.620701">
    <name>Arosa (Graubunden) [from 53 CHF]</name>
    <desc>Hoernligrat 2496 m - top of the Hoernli-Express

    Trails
The high, open, quieter half of the Bike Kingdom. The Hoernli Trail is the classic - over 6 km of flowing alpine singletrack from the Hoernligrat back to the village - with the Aelplisee and Schwellisee trails threading past the lakes below the Weisshorn. Less built and more mountain than Lenzerheide; the Arosa Lenzerheide Rundtour ties the two resorts into one big day.

    Getting up / price
Same Bike Kingdom ticket as Lenzerheide, from 53 CHF, and the Urdenbahn links the two sides so you can ride both on one pass. Note the Arosa Card discount is only sold at Arosa counters.

    Open season
Open from 15 June; closed from 26 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train | ~4h45

    Source: Arosa Lenzerheide.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.789284" lon="9.639157">
    <name>Arosa: Weisshorn 2653 m</name>
    <desc>Top of the Weisshornbahn, the high point above the village and the start of the long alpine descents.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.782947" lon="9.678332">
    <name>Arosa: village lift hub</name>
    <desc>Arosa station is the end of the RhB rack line from Chur - step off the train and you are at the lifts.</desc>
  </wpt>
