  <wpt lat="45.247142" lon="6.018802">
    <name>Les 7 Laux - Prapoutel (Belledonne) [21.50 EUR online]</name>
    <desc>Chamois - top of the chairlift

    Trails
The other side of the Belledonne from Chamrousse, and the rowdier of the two. A dense set of numbered descents - Or'Anjina, Bel'Dina, Jasse and Cortillets for flow, Bloody Roots and Bloody Rock for the rough stuff, Mini Shore and Chevre Shore for woodwork. Steep, rooty and often damp under the trees, with a long run-out all the way to Froges in the valley if you want the full 1100 m.

Rain sensitivity
Rain-sensitive: rooty, shaded forest terrain stays damp and becomes slippery quickly after rain.

    Getting up / price
Day pass 21.50 EUR online, 23.50 EUR at the window; 4 hours 18 EUR, two days 37.50 EUR, six days 67 EUR. Lifts run 4 July to 30 August 2026, and the Bouquetins and Chamois chairlifts alternate rather than both running every day.

    Open season
Open from 4 July; closed from 31 August (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Grenoble | Car | ~50 min

    Source: Les 7 Laux.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.251177" lon="6.001611">
    <name>7 Laux: Bouquetins</name>
    <desc>Second chairlift. The two do not always run on the same days - check which one is turning before you drive up.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.256216" lon="5.995404">
