  <wpt lat="45.111100" lon="5.608300">
    <name>Lans-en-Vercors (Vercors) [check the lift]</name>
    <desc>Bachassons - Montagnes de Lans lift area

    Trails
A compact, friendly set of built descents in the trees on the Vercors plateau: La Bleue is the easy one, Bois Sigu and La Croix des Suifs step it up. Limestone rather than granite, so it rides fast when dry and greasy when not. Worth combining with the Via Vercors network if the lift is shut.

Rain sensitivity
Rain-sensitive: limestone and forest soil get greasy rapidly when wet.

    Getting up / price
The nearest bike park to Grenoble as the crow flies, but the one to phone ahead about: summer chairlift operation at Lans is not guaranteed the way it is at Chamrousse, and the season is short. Worst case it is a pedal-up, and the climb is not long.

    Open season
Open from 1 July; closed from 1 September (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Grenoble | Car | ~35 min

    Source: Lans-en-Vercors tourism.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
