  <wpt lat="45.029800" lon="5.569300">
    <name>Villard-de-Lans / Correncon (Vercors) [see operator]</name>
    <desc>Cote 2000 - top of the gondola

    Trails
A proper DH and enduro area on the Villard-Correncon domain, reached by the Cote 2000 gondola. Limestone plateau riding with big open pasture up top and steep wooded sections lower down - less alpine than Belledonne, more technical than it looks. The Vercors weather is its own thing: it can be clagged in here while Chamrousse bakes.

    Getting up / price
Usually the first bike park in France to open, in early June. Weekends in June and September, then daily 5 July to 31 August, 9:00-17:00. The operator publishes a summer price grid at villardcorrencon.com, budget in line with its neighbours, roughly 20-25 EUR a day.

    Open season
Open from 5 July; closed from 1 September (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Published operating hours; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Grenoble | Car | ~45 min

    Source: Villard-Correncon.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.044400" lon="5.560000">
    <name>Villard: Cote 2000 valley station</name>
    <desc>The gondola takes three bikes and riders per cabin, so expect a queue on a hot Sunday in August.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.049700" lon="5.563000">
    <name>Villard: Glovettes</name>
    <desc>Second lift sector above the village.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.677656" lon="7.178790">
    <name>La Berra (Fribourg Prealps) [37 CHF / Magic Pass]</name>
    <desc>La Berra 1719 m - top of the gondola

    Trails
Berra Bike Park: two purpose-built descents totalling about 9 km. Les Allieres is the blue one, 5.6 km of berms, smooth sections and small jumps looking out over the Prealps - one of the best beginner-to-intermediate flow runs in French-speaking Switzerland. La Tschaka is the red: technical features, steeper banks and real jumps. Small, well kept, and rarely busy midweek.

    Getting up / price
Bike day pass 37 CHF, single ascent 17 CHF, pedestrian return 23 CHF. Free with the Magic Pass. Season 1 July to 31 October, daily from 09:00, with late evening running from mid-July to mid-September.

    Open season
Open from 1 July; closed from 1 November (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Published opening time; closing time is estimated.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train + bus | ~1h50

    Source: La Berra.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.686608" lon="7.154978">
    <name>La Berra: Le Brand valley station</name>
    <desc>Base of the telemixte at La Roche. The cabins are equipped to carry bikes, so you can lap without pedalling up.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <trk>
    <name>La Robella: La Carabosse</name>
    <desc>Official 3 km difficult downhill from La Robella to Buttes, with 480 m of descent: approximately 2 km of demanding singletrack and 1 km of asphalt/access track. Expect technical obstacles and large jumps, although the operator says every feature can be bypassed. A sighting lap, full-face helmet and body protection are strongly recommended.

Geometry follows the five MTB downhill sections mapped in OpenStreetMap ways 919395620, 285345983, 285345990, 285341626 and 285240316, joined along mapped access tracks (ODbL). Indicative only; follow the signs on the ground.

Sources: La Robella and SwitzerlandMobility route 10004.</desc>
