  <wpt lat="46.875975" lon="6.548741">
    <name>La Robella Bike Park [magic pass, from 27 CHF]</name>
    <desc>La Robella 1220 m - top of the Buttes-La Robella chairlift

    Trails
The lift serves La Carabosse, an official difficult downhill to Buttes: 3 km and 480 m of descent, including around 2 km of technical singletrack with jumps and obstacles. The station also suggests several unmarked touring and e-MTB loops; its blue, red and black all-terrain scooter routes are not MTB downhill trails.

    Getting up / price
Chairlift access. The adult bike day pass is 27 CHF and bike transport is free. Magic Pass is accepted.

    Open season
Typically open from mid-May to late October, with daily operation in peak summer and reduced opening outside it. Check the current schedule and conditions.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train + bus | ~1h30

    Sources: La Robella downhill, official prices and SwitzerlandMobility.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.251400" lon="7.510300">
    <name>Weissenstein (Solothurn) [gondola, from 38 CHF]</name>
    <desc>Weissenstein 1284 m - top of the gondola

    Trails
Natural, technical freeride/enduro descent running down the Weissenstein mountain toward Oberdorf. Steep gradient, tight switchbacks, slick forest soil, exposed roots, and limestone rock features. Best suited for advanced riders who appreciate raw mountain trails.

Rain sensitivity
Rain-sensitive: slick forest soil and exposed roots become difficult quickly after rain.

    Getting up / price
Gondola access (Seilbahn Weissenstein). Bike single ride or day pass options available; day ticket is approximately 38-48 CHF (including bike transport).

    Open season
Open from May; closed from late October (subject to trail weather conditions and snow melt).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train | ~1h50

    Source: Seilbahn Weissenstein.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.243500" lon="7.258100">
    <name>Bike Park Valbirse [from 15 CHF]</name>
    <desc>Téléski Les Orvales 1065 m - top of the surface lift

    Trails
Compact, community-maintained bike park featuring technical singletracks, flow sections with tabletop jumps, bermed turns, and short jump lines (Expresso, Chilli Peppers, Schtroumpfette). Small scale but well-loved local spot in the Bernese Jura.

    Getting up / price
Surface T-bar drag lift (Téléski Les Orvales). Operating hours are managed by the local club; day pass typically costs around 15-25 CHF.

    Open season
Open from late April/early May; closed from late October (typical window; check the local club).
Daily opening hours: variable
Check the local club schedule before visiting.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train | ~1h50

    Sources: BikePark Valbirse, official hours and prices, Commune de Valbirse, Trailforks trail directory.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.853200" lon="7.904800">
    <name>Marbachegg Bike Park [from 38 CHF]</name>
    <desc>Marbachegg 1500 m - top of the gondola

    Trails
Home to the Clientis Flowtrail and CKW Jump Trail. The main flow trail drops ~400 meters of elevation over 4.5 km, featuring swooping curves, rollers, table jumps, and wooden step-downs suitable for intermediate and advanced riders. Beautiful setting in the Entlebuch Biosphere.

    Getting up / price
Gondola access (Sportbahnen Marbachegg). A bike day pass is around 38-42 CHF.

    Open season
Open from mid-May; closed from late October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lucerne | Train + bus | ~1h30
Lausanne | Train | ~2h30

    Source: Marbachegg.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.661000" lon="7.298200">
    <name>Schwarzsee - Riggisalp (Kaiseregg) [from 32 CHF]</name>
    <desc>Riggisalp 1500 m - top of the chairlift

    Trails
Mix of alpine freeride trails and singletracks leading down from Riggisalp to the lake. The terrain blends fast open alpine pastures, rocky paths, root-filled forest sections, and natural bank turns. Spectacular Fribourg Pre-Alps setting.

    Getting up / price
2-seater chairlift (Sesselbahn Riggisalp). Day ticket with unlimited bike transport is approximately 32-38 CHF.

    Open season
Open from late May; closed from late October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train + bus | ~1h45

    Source: Schwarzsee.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.919547" lon="7.439742">
    <name>Gurten (Bern) [city fare + 3.50 CHF bike]</name>
    <desc>Gurten Kulm 858 m - top of the funicular

    Trails
GurtenTrail 2.0, rebuilt from scratch in 2025: 2.5 km and 240 m of descent with around 40 jumps, endless berms and a lot of thought in the shaping. Every feature is rollable, so beginners can ride the whole thing, while the line choices and doubles keep it interesting if you can send. Free bike wash on the third floor of the car park at the bottom.

    Getting up / price
Bern's local hill, so it is city transport pricing: take the S-Bahn or tram to Wabern, then the Gurtenbahn funicular. A bike ticket is 3.50 CHF per ride on top of your own fare, and the trail itself is free. Runs all year, every 15 minutes, which is what makes this a genuine winter option.

    Open season
Open from 1 January with no seasonal closure (normally open year-round).
Daily opening hours: 07:00-23:30
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train + funicular | ~1h20

    Source: Gurtenbahn.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
