  <wpt lat="46.698232" lon="7.855001">
    <name>Interlaken - Harder Kulm [funicular, price unverified]</name>
    <desc>Harder Kulm 1322 m - top of the funicular

    Trails
The Harder Downhill: a steep, relentless 700 m drop off Interlaken's local peak straight back into town. Tight, rooty switchbacks through the forest with a couple of genuinely exposed sections - not a first bike park, but the view over the Thunersee and Brienzersee on the way up is worth the ticket on its own.

    Getting up / price
The Harderbahn funicular leaves a few minutes' walk from Interlaken Ost. Bike carriage is limited and the 2026 fare is not confirmed here - check jungfrau.ch, and note the funicular is primarily a tourist ride, so expect queues at midday.

    Open season
Open from 1 April; closed from 1 December (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-21:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train | ~2h20

    Source: Jungfrau Railways.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
