  <wpt lat="46.017290" lon="7.770060">
    <name>Zermatt - Sunnegga [~55 CHF]</name>
    <desc>Sunnegga 2285 m - top of the Sunnegga Express funicular

    Trails
Zermatt wraps a bike park in four-thousand-metre scenery. The Sunnegga-Trail (blue) is a 7 km flow descent all the way to town; the Riffelberg Trail is a 6.5 km natural enduro line with Matterhorn views the whole way down. The Moos-Trail and short connectors around the Sunnegga-Blauherd mid-station give you extra variety before the final drop to the village. Most routes funnel back to the high street, so the apres-ride pizza is 30 seconds from the bottom.

    Getting up / price
Sunnegga Express (underground funicular) carries bikes inside the cabin. Day bike pass around 55 CHF - price not verified here; check zermatt.ch before travelling.

    Open season
Open from 15 June; closed from 19 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train | ~2h30

    Source: Zermatt.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
