  <wpt lat="46.093220" lon="7.533680">
    <name>La Forclaz - Le Tsaté (Val d'Hérens) [small t-bar]</name>
    <desc>Le Tsaté 2200 m - top of the t-bar

    Trails
A tiny, old-school bike spot on a south-facing slope above Evolène. Two surface lifts - a platter and a t-bar - drag you and your bike up to just above 2200 m, and you drop back through larch forest and open pasture on natural, unsurfaced singletrack. No bike park features, no crowd, just a quiet local run with views of the Dent Blanche and the Val d'Hérens. The restaurant at the bottom does a solid croûte au fromage.

    Getting up / price
Small t-bar (téléski du Tsaté) and platter lift - bikes tag along on a hook. Day pass around 15-20 CHF; price not verified here. Check with the Evolène tourist office before travelling.

    Open season
Open from 1 May; closed from 1 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train + bus | ~2h15

    Source: Evolène Région Tourisme.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.091570" lon="7.516580">
    <name>La Forclaz: bottom of Le Tsaté t-bar</name>
    <desc>Bottom station of the Le Tsaté t-bar at 1695 m. Access road, parking and the restaurant.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <trk>
    <name>La Forclaz: Les Rocs Bike Tour</name>
    <desc>25 km expert MTB loop with about 1,044 m of climbing. It crosses Les Hauderes and La Forclaz, climbs through the Tsate, Prelet and Cotter alpine pastures, then follows a technical descent towards Villaz and La Sage through high forest, traditional villages and open mountain scenery. This is a demanding pedal-up tour, not a lift-served downhill run. Source: Evolene Region - Les Rocs Bike Tour. Official GPX geometry supplied by Evolene Region, simplified to 20 m.</desc>
