  <wpt lat="46.772374" lon="6.466241">
    <name>Le Suchet (Jura vaudois) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Le Suchet 1588 m - summit

    Trails
Open Jura ridge with descents falling off every side - grassy and fast on the Vaud slope, rockier and steeper towards Baulmes. No signage, no lift queue, big views over the Plateau to the Alps. Best in early summer before the cattle churn the tracks.

    Getting up / price
No lift. Yverdon-les-Bains is 25 min from Lausanne, then a bus to Baulmes or Vuiteboeuf. From there it is roughly 800 m of climbing under your own steam.

    Open season
Open from 15 April; closed from 16 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions).

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train + bus | ~1h15

    Source: Swiss federal map.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.572227" lon="6.276140">
    <name>Grand Cunay / Col du Marchairuz [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Grand Cunay 1566 m

    Trails
Classic Jura vaudois ridge riding above the Vallee de Joux. Rolling limestone pasture, dry-stone walls and forest singletrack, with long low-gradient descents rather than steep ones. Quiet on weekdays; the Parc Jura vaudois rules ask you to stay on the tracks.

    Getting up / price
No lift, and a sparse bus timetable: check the Bière or Le Brassus connections to the Col du Marchairuz before committing. Many people ride up from Bière instead.

    Open season
Open from 15 April; closed from 16 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions).

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Train + bus | ~1h30

    Source: Swiss federal map.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <trk>
    <name>Le Chasseron: Chasseron Bike 987</name>
    <desc>34 km official, signposted MTB loop from Sainte-Croix via Mont de la Mayaz, the 1607 m Chasseron summit and Les Cluds. It combines 10 km of singletrack with natural-surface and paved linking sections; medium technical difficulty but demanding fitness with about 1200 m of climbing and descent. Source: Jura &amp; Trois-Lacs / SwitzerlandMobility. Official GPX geometry supplied by the Commune of Bullet, simplified to 8 m.</desc>
