  <wpt lat="46.565724" lon="6.692604">
    <name>Chalet-a-Gobet / Jorat (Lausanne) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Chalet-a-Gobet - Jorat forest trailhead

    Trails
The after-work option: a dense web of forest doubletrack and singletrack across the Jorat, ridable in any weather and floodlit by nothing at all, so bring lights in winter. No descents worth travelling for, but 20 minutes from your door and the trails drain well.

Rain sensitivity
Rain-resilient: the Jorat forest network drains well and is regularly rideable in mixed weather.

    Getting up / price
No lift and none needed - it is only 400 m above the city. Bus 64 from Lausanne, or the m2 to Croisettes and pedal up.

    Open season
Open from 1 January with no seasonal closure in a typical year; check local conditions.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Bus / metro + bus | ~25 min

    Source: Lausanne tourism.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.688440" lon="7.310960">
    <name>Pila Bike Park (Aosta Valley) [40 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Pila 1790 m - Aosta-Pila gondola top station

    Trails
A large, natural-feeling gravity area above Aosta with more than 130 km of riding and 2100 m of vertical. The official 2026 park lists one blue flow trail, twelve red descents, three black trails and the black Corrado Herin World Cup line, plus the long freeride descent back to Aosta.

    Getting up / price
The 2026 adult bike pass is 40 EUR and includes bike transport. The Aosta-Pila gondola and bike park run daily from 13 June to 13 September 2026; Chamole opens from 20 June.

    Open season
Open from 13 June; closed from 14 September (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Car | ~3h00
Aosta | Gondola | ~18 min

    Source: Pila.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
