  <wpt lat="43.802400" lon="7.458455">
    <name>Menton - St Agnes - Col de la Madone - Peille [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Sainte-Agnes 800 m - pedal-access trail hub above Menton

    Trails
A broad natural enduro area linking Sainte-Agnes, Castillon, Col de la Madone, Peille and Gorbio. Historic paths and technical singletrack can be linked into longer rides, including the red GR51 descent from Sainte-Agnes to Monti and the black Ravin du Rank from Col de la Madone toward Gorbio. The Ravin drops about 550 m over 2.8 km and is graded T5 / E2, with loose limestone, stone steps and exposed sections.

    Getting up / price
No lift and no trail fee. Climb by road from Menton, Sainte-Agnes, Gorbio or Peille; shuttling by car is possible for some lines.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; Ravin du Rank is T5 and exposed. Scout the step sections before committing.

    Open season
Open year-round in a typical year; check weather, wildfire restrictions and local trail access.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Menton | Bike | ~1 h climb
Nice | Car | ~50 min

    Sources: VTTour Ravin du Rank, VTTour Sainte-Agnes - Monti, and the linked OpenStreetMap trail geometries (ODbL). Routes and access can change; verify locally.</desc>
  </wpt>
