  <wpt lat="33.705273" lon="35.702272">
    <name>Chouf - Barouk Cedar Reserve MTB (Lebanon) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Natural mountain riding around Barouk and the Chouf

    Trails
The Chouf is one of Lebanon's best-known mountain-bike regions, with long climbs and descents on rough tracks between Barouk, Maasser el Chouf, cedar forest and exposed Mount Lebanon ridges. The attraction is backcountry scenery and endurance-oriented natural riding, not purpose-built gravity trails.

    Getting up / price
No lift. Pedal the routes or arrange guide and vehicle support. The cedar reserve is protected: bicycles may be restricted to designated roads and routes, so confirm the exact itinerary with reserve staff.

    Open season
Open from 01 May; closed from 01 December (typical snow-free window).
Daily opening hours: daylight hours
Reserve hours, security conditions, snow and fire restrictions can change.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Beirut | Car | ~1h15
Barouk | Bike | ~20 min

    Sources: official Lebanon tourism cycling guidance and the Shouf Biosphere Reserve. Confirm bicycle permissions and current local conditions before riding.</desc>
  </wpt>
