  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="56.191598" lon="9.573603">
    <name>Silkeborg BikePark (Denmark) [free, no lift]</name>
    <desc>Progressive municipal jump and flow park

    Trails
Silkeborg's MTB playground uses ski-style colour grading. A rollable green flow line leads toward blue and red jump progression, while the black jump line has four large, steep tables and closely spaced expert features.

    Getting up / price
Free and pedal- or push-accessed; no lift. Walk unfamiliar jump lines before riding.

    Open season
Open from 01 January; closed from 01 January (normally year-round).
Daily opening hours: daylight hours
Avoid riding when wet or when local closures are posted.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Silkeborg station | Bike | ~15 min
Aarhus | Train + bike | ~1h00

    Source: VisitDenmark / VisitAarhus. Check local conditions before riding.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="56.831338" lon="9.871925">
    <name>Rold Skov Trailcenter (Denmark) [free, no lift]</name>
    <desc>Denmark's largest technical forest MTB network

    Trails
Around 50 km and roughly 1000 m of cumulative climbing cover blue, red, black and extreme grades. The network mixes flowing singletrack, roots and punchy climbs with a dedicated skills area and Denmark's largest downhill track, a 450 m orange line dropping about 45 m.

    Getting up / price
Free and pedal-accessed; no lift. Routes start near Skorping Hallen and must be ridden in the marked direction.

    Open season
Open from 01 January; closed from 01 January (normally year-round).
Daily opening hours: daylight hours
Respect Nature Agency rules and avoid damaging saturated or frozen trails.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Aalborg | Train + bike | ~35 min
Skorping station | Bike | ~5 min

    Source: Danish Nature Agency. Follow current forestry notices.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="56.976038" lon="8.506063">
    <name>Thy MTB Park (Denmark) [free, no lift]</name>
    <desc>Purpose-built trail centre in the Thy forest landscape

    Trails
Three marked MTB routes form a compact destination for half- or full-day riding in the sandy, wooded terrain of northwest Jutland. The emphasis is flowing natural singletrack and trail-centre riding rather than large elevation, with options for mixed abilities.

    Getting up / price
Free and pedal-accessed; no lift.

    Open season
Open from 01 January; closed from 01 January (normally year-round).
Daily opening hours: daylight hours
Check forestry notices and trail conditions, especially after severe weather.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Thisted | Car / bike | ~20 min
Aalborg | Car | ~1h30

    Source: VisitDenmark. Follow local trail signs and closures.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="42.893056" lon="140.699722">
    <name>Niseko Hanazono Mountain Bike Park (Hokkaido) [3800 JPY]</name>
    <desc>Hanazono gondola - lift-accessed Niseko flow trails

    Trails
A new purpose-built gravity park opened in July 2026, designed by Allegra with local supervision from NAMBA. Hanazono Skyline is a 4.2 km blue flow descent with about 347 m of vertical; the free 1.36 km Mori Loop gives beginners a gentler introduction near the base.

    Getting up / price
The Hanazono gondola carries bikes. Adult day pass 3800 JPY, child 2500 JPY; adult season pass 28000 JPY. Rentals and protective equipment are available.

    Open season
Open from 1 July; closed from 12 October (2026 opening date and estimated autumn closing window).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:00
Closing date and daily hours are estimates; check the operator schedule and trail status.

    Sources: Niseko Hanazono and NAMBA.
    Prices, schedules and conditions can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="42.861965" lon="140.697889">
    <name>Niseko Grand Hirafu MTB Park (Hokkaido) [4000 JPY]</name>
    <desc>Ace gondola - lift-accessed flow above Hirafu

    Trails
A renewed 4.4 km intermediate-to-advanced flow trail descends the ski slopes, with berms, rollers and faster technical sections. A separate free skills area at the base provides beginner and intermediate progression terrain.

    Getting up / price
The Ace gondola carries bikes. Adult day pass 4000 JPY, child 2500 JPY; adult season pass 30000 JPY. The skills area is free.

    Open season
Open from 4 July; closed from 28 September (published 2026 dates; September is weekends and holidays only, and 6 September is closed for an event).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-16:00; last ascent 15:30
Published 2026 schedule; check weather and trail status.

    Source: Niseko Tokyu Grand Hirafu.
    Prices, schedules and conditions can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="42.873000" lon="140.706500">
    <name>Twin Peaks Bike Park (Niseko, Hokkaido) [free, no lift]</name>
    <desc>Free community trail network above Hirafu

    Trails
Japan's largest free-access bike park has more than 17 km across 20 professionally built trails. Five green trails lead into blue flow, rock-and-root black lines and the double-black Taki Tech. Most descents are bike-specific and one-way, while several connectors are shared with other users.

    Getting up / price
Free. No lift and no shuttle: use the purpose-built climbing trails. The nonprofit NAMBA manages the network and publishes live wet-trail status; do not ride closed or saturated trails.

    Open season
Open from 15 May; closed from 1 November (published mid-May to end-October window).
Daily opening hours: 07:00-19:00
Check NAMBA for current trail conditions.

    Source: NAMBA Twin Peaks. Access and conditions can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="36.906680" lon="138.452555">
    <name>Nozawa Onsen MTB Park (Nagano) [gondola, price varies]</name>
    <desc>Nagasaka gondola - long gravity laps above Nozawa Onsen

    Trails
About 10 km of downhill courses range from beginner and intermediate flow to advanced natural terrain, using the ski hill's large vertical and wooded lower slopes. Rentals are available at Nagasaka Center House.

    Getting up / price
The Nagasaka gondola carries riders and bikes. The operator publishes ticket options seasonally; check the current MTB tariff before travelling.

    Open season
Open from 18 July; closed from 26 October (published 2026 dates). From 25 August to 17 September it is closed Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday.
Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:30; last gondola ascent 16:00
Published 2026 schedule; weather closures are possible.

    Source: Nozawa Onsen Mountain Resort.
    Prices, schedules and conditions can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="36.863338" lon="138.135747">
    <name>Myoko Suginohara MTB (Niigata) [gondola, details unverified]</name>
    <desc>Suginohara gondola - riding on the flank of Mount Myoko

    Trails
Green-season riding uses forest and ski-area terrain around the long Suginohara gondola, with gondola-served downhill described by Japan's national tourism guide. Expect natural mountain riding rather than a large, fully signed modern bike park.

    Getting up / price
The Suginohara gondola has carried mountain bikes, but a current 2026 MTB operating calendar and tariff could not be confirmed. Contact the resort before making a dedicated trip.

    Open season
Open from 1 July; closed from 1 November (estimated summer-to-autumn window).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:00
Season and hours are estimates; confirm bike carriage and current trail access with the operator.

    Sources: Japan National Tourism Organization and Myoko Suginohara. Operations can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="36.672167" lon="137.821999">
    <name>Hakuba 47 Mountain Bike Park (Nagano) [1200 JPY, no lift]</name>
    <desc>Beginner-focused trail and skills park at the Hakuba 47 base

    Trails
Three main trails and an absolute-beginner practice area focus on accessible progression: gentle singletrack, rollers, berm-like turns, rocks, narrow-path practice and a children's course. Bikes and protection can be rented at the resort.

    Getting up / price
Current park trails are in the base area and are ridden under pedal power. Entry with your own bike is 1200 JPY for a day or 600 JPY for two hours; rental packages include park entry.

    Open season
Open from 17 July; closed from 24 September (2026 opening date and estimated late-September closing window; closed 24-26 July for a private event).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:00
Closing date and daily hours are estimates; check the resort before travel.

    Sources: Hakuba 47 MTB and the 2026 summer page.
    Prices, schedules and conditions can change.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="6.992289" lon="80.418823">
    <name>Downhill MTB Kitulgala (Sri Lanka) [truck shuttle]</name>
    <desc>Purpose-built tropical gravity trail at Kitulgala

    Trails
Sri Lanka's dedicated downhill MTB operation combines purpose-built and natural trail through lush forest and villages. The guided three-hour experience starts with induction and practice, then follows a gravity descent suitable for beginners through experienced riders, ending with a river swim.

    Getting up / price
A truck shuttles riders to the top, so there is no uphill pedalling. Bikes, helmet, safety equipment and assistance are included in the booked experience. Pricing varies by booking date and group; reserve with the operator.

    Open season
Open from 1 January; closed from 1 January (operates by reservation year-round, subject to rain and trail conditions).
Daily opening hours: 08:00-17:00
Typical booking window; confirm the meeting time and conditions directly.

    Sources: Downhill MTB Sri Lanka and its linked booking information. Availability and prices can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="7.525000" lon="80.783300">
    <name>Knuckles Mountain Range - Riverston (Sri Lanka) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <desc>Highland adventure riding around Riverston Pass

    Trails
Long guided cross-country and enduro-style days combine steep backroads, estate tracks and permitted paths around Riverston and the edge of the Knuckles range. Expect mist, exposed viewpoints, rough surfaces and a large amount of climbing rather than a signed gravity park.

    Getting up / price
No lift. Tours commonly use vehicle support but the riding itself includes substantial pedalling. This is a protected World Heritage landscape: do not assume hiking-only paths permit bicycles, use a knowledgeable local guide, and confirm the exact route and conservation access before riding.

    Open season
Open from 1 December; closed from 1 May (typical drier riding window; rain is possible year-round).
Daily opening hours: daylight hours
Access is route-dependent; confirm permissions, weather and guide arrangements locally.

    Sources: SL Voyo mountain-bike tour, Central Province Tourism and Riverston activities. Conditions and permitted access can change.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="35.904970" lon="138.181230">
    <name>Fujimi Panorama (Nagano, Japan) [5500 JPY]</name>
    <desc>Summit 1780 m - top of the Suzuran gondola

    Trails
Japan's best-known downhill hill, on the flank of the Yatsugatake with the Southern Alps across the valley. Courses run from a wide beginner flow line to steep, rooty and rutted expert tracks; the longest links 8 km of trail for 730 m of descent, which makes for laps that punish arms rather than legs. A separate gentle skill-improvement area sits at the base for anyone starting out.

    Getting up / price
The Suzuran gondola lifts riders and bikes from 1055 m to the 1780 m summit in around 10 minutes; two pair lifts serve the lower courses. One-day gondola and lift pass 5500 JPY adult, 2800 JPY child; the skill area alone is 2500 JPY. The 2026 season runs 24 April to 15 November.

    Open season
Open from 24 April; closed from 16 November (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-16:30
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Tokyo | Train + shuttle | ~3h00
Fujimi station | Shuttle | ~10 min

    Source: Fujimi Panorama.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
