  <wpt lat="47.410790" lon="12.714450">
    <name>Bikepark Leogang - Asitz (Salzburg) [66 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Asitz 1755 m - top of the Asitzbahn

    Trails
The World Cup hill, and the one most riders mean when they say Austria. Hangman II is the race track, steep and rooty into the finish arena; Riderman and Speedster are the long, jump-heavy signature lines; the Flying Gangster and the wood-built sections keep it from being just another mountainside. There is a genuine green progression line and a skills area at the bottom, so it is not only a park for people who already send.

    Getting up / price
The Asitzbahn gondola runs in two sections from Leogang at 835 m, with the Asitzgipfelbahn continuing to 1860 m. Day pass 66 EUR adult in main season, 56 EUR for four hours; prices are dynamic and cheaper booked online. Season pass 449 EUR, and it also covers Saalbach Hinterglemm, Fieberbrunn and the Kitzsteinhorn. Open 8 May to 8 November 2026.

    Open season
Open from 8 May; closed from 9 November (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-16:30
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Salzburg | Car | ~1h00
Munich | Car | ~2h00

    Source: Bikepark Leogang.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.439250" lon="12.718830">
    <name>Leogang: Asitzbahn valley station (835 m)</name>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.405770" lon="12.707480">
    <name>Leogang: Asitzgipfelbahn top (1860 m)</name>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.367880" lon="12.637990">
    <name>Saalbach Hinterglemm - Schattberg (Salzburg) [39 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Schattberg Ost 2010 m - top of the Schattberg X-Press

    Trails
The other half of the Epic Bikepark, and the one that rewards riding all day rather than lapping one line. Over 36 km of park trail plus a dozen singletracks spread across both sides of a long valley, so you can cross the whole thing on lifts. The Hacklbergtrail from the Schattberg is the classic: 6 km and 600 m of descent of natural, flowing singletrack rather than berms. The Reiterkogel side holds the built lines - Blue Line, X-Line, Pro Line - and 18 km of new trail opened at Schoenleiten for 2026.

    Getting up / price
The Schattberg X-Press lifts bikes in two sections out of Saalbach at 990 m; a dozen other lifts carry bikes across the valley. Day pass 39 EUR adult, cheaper booked online, and free discounts apply with a JOKER CARD from local accommodation. The Leogang season pass is valid here.

    Open season
Open from 15 May; closed from 27 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-16:30
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Salzburg | Car | ~1h15

    Source: Saalbach.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
