    <name>Hinterglemm: Reiterkogelbahn, built lines (1475 m)</name>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.373000" lon="13.724390">
    <name>Bikepark Schladming - Planai (Styria) [58.50 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Planai 1820 m - top of the Planaibahn

    Trails
42 km of trail down a single big face, and the one Austrian park with real World Cup history under it. The 2.5 km World Cup downhill runs from the mid-station to the valley and links out of the 2.6 km Downhill Pro above it, which is as serious as Austrian racing gets. Everything else is built for airtime or for learning: the Flowline, the 99 Jumpline, the Monster Jumpline, and a Rookie Trail that actually works as a first descent.

    Getting up / price
The Planaibahn gondola runs in two sections from Schladming at 740 m. Day pass 58.50 EUR adult, 44.50 EUR youth. Open daily 29 May to 21 September 2026, then Thursday to Sunday until 5 October. The Gravity Card is accepted.

    Open season
Open from 29 May; closed from 6 October (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-16:30
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Salzburg | Car | ~1h20
Vienna | Car | ~3h30

    Source: Schladming-Dachstein.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.392890" lon="13.693220">
    <name>Schladming: Planaibahn valley station (740 m)</name>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.059590" lon="10.592420">
    <name>Bikepark Serfaus-Fiss-Ladis (Tirol) [38.50 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Moeseralm 1820 m - top of the Moeseralmbahn, Fiss

    Trails
Nine park trails from green to black, and the reason to come: two of the longest singletracks in the Alps drop off the ridge above. The Frommestrail runs 9.8 km for 900 m of descent, and the Zirbentrail 9.1 km through stone pine forest, both starting from the Schoenjoch at 2420 m. Down at the valley station there is a kids park, a pumptrack and a slopestyle zone, which makes this the best of the Austrian parks to bring a family to.

    Getting up / price
The Moeseralmbahn gondola from Fiss serves the park trails; the Schoenjochbahn continues to 2420 m for the long singletracks. Day pass 38.50 EUR adult, 33 EUR from midday. Lifts 8:30 to 17:00, season 13 June to 11 October 2026.

    Open season
Open from 13 June; closed from 12 October (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00
Published operating hours; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Innsbruck | Car | ~1h15

    Source: Bikepark Serfaus-Fiss-Ladis.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
