  <wpt lat="46.975260" lon="10.975980">
    <name>Bike Republic Soelden (Oetztal, Tirol) [39 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Giggijoch 2270 m - top of the Giggijochbahn

    Trails
High-alpine riding above the tree line, which almost nowhere else on this map offers on a lift ticket. 33 shaped lines over 42 km, and more than 70 km once the singletracks and enduro routes are counted. The Teaere Line is the flagship flow descent; the Gahe Line is the one people come back with stories about. Two separate lift systems, Giggijoch and Gaislachkogl, open different halves of the mountain.

    Getting up / price
The Giggijochbahn and Gaislachkoglbahn gondolas both take bikes and both sell tickets. Day pass 39 EUR adult, 28 EUR from 11:30. Being at 2270 m, the season is short and weather-dependent - check the lift status before driving up the Oetztal.

    Open season
Open from 12 June; closed from 5 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-16:30
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
