  <wpt lat="47.211570" lon="11.333710">
    <name>Bikepark Innsbruck - Muttereralm (Tirol) [57 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Muttereralm 1600 m - top of the Muttereralmbahn

    Trails
Ten trails over about 20 km, ten minutes from the middle of Innsbruck, which makes this the easiest world-class riding to reach without a car on the whole map. Blue flow through to black downhill race track, an extended top section and connectors between the lines, plus a Rookie Park with an airbag. Across the valley, the Nordkette Singletrail drops off the Seegrube at 1900 m and has a reputation as one of the hardest marked descents in Europe - a different lift, a different ticket, and not a beginner's afternoon.

    Getting up / price
The Muttereralmbahn gondola from Mutters, reachable by tram from Innsbruck. Day pass 57 EUR at the window, from 44 EUR booked online at least three days ahead. Daily 9:00 to 17:00, late May to late October.

    Open season
Open from 25 May; closed from 26 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Published operating hours; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Innsbruck | Tram + gondola | ~35 min

    Source: Bikepark Innsbruck.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
