  <wpt lat="46.859010" lon="9.847830">
    <name>Davos Klosters - Gotschna (Graubunden) [60 CHF]</name>
    <desc>Gotschnagrat 2280 m - top of the Gotschnabahn

    Trails
The Gotschna Freeride is the gravity draw: 5.8 km and 590 m of descent, more than 200 banked turns and thirty-odd tables, built in the spirit of Whistler's A-Line and maintained to the same standard. Across the valley the Jakobshorn holds the Ischalp flow trail, about 7 km for 1000 m of descent, plus a technique trail that works as a genuine first day out.

    Getting up / price
The Gotschnabahn cable car from Klosters at 1190 m. A day pass including bike transport is about 60 CHF; the bike surcharge alone is 15 CHF, and a bike summer season pass is 160 CHF.

    Open season
Open from 15 June; closed from 20 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

