    <name>Scuol - Motta Naluns (Unterengadin) [lift pass, price unverified]</name>
    <desc>Motta Naluns 2145 m - top of the Scuol gondola

    Trails
The quiet one. Ten marked mountain-bike routes fan out from Motta Naluns, two easy, two intermediate, three advanced and three hard, and they are natural trails cut into the hillside rather than shaped berms. 850 m of descent back to Scuol, and the Unterengadin gets a lot more sun and a lot fewer riders than Graubunden's headline parks. Finish in the Scuol thermal baths.

    Getting up / price
The Scuol gondola carries bikes, as do the Ftan and Naluns chairlifts. The operator publishes its summer tariff on bergbahnen-scuol.ch; we could not confirm a 2026 bike day rate, so check before you go.

    Open season
Open from 15 June; closed from 19 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Zurich | Train | ~3h00
Landeck | Car | ~1h00

    Source: Engadin Scuol.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.795320" lon="10.289130">
    <name>Scuol: gondola valley station (1295 m)</name>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.778750" lon="8.386750">
    <name>Engelberg - Jochpass (Obwalden) [42 CHF]</name>
    <desc>Jochpass 2205 m - top of the Jochpass chairlift

    Trails
The Jochpass Trail is the reason to come: 4.5 km of flowtrail from the pass down to Trubsee, gentle curves and small jumps, with no technical difficulty and a genuinely spectacular setting under the Titlis. Lower down, the Hells-Bells Trail adds 1.6 km with berms and a few harder sections. Not a big park, but a very good day, and easy to reach from Lucerne without a car.

    Getting up / price
The Titlis Xpress gondola from Engelberg at 1000 m to Trubsee, then the Jochpass chairlift. MTB day pass 42 CHF for 16 and over, 21 CHF for 6 to 15, valid Engelberg - Trubsee - Jochpass - Engstlenalp.

    Open season
Open from 15 June; closed from 19 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lucerne | Train | ~45 min
Zurich | Train | ~1h45

    Source: Engelberg.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.793500" lon="8.397670">
    <name>Engelberg: Trubsee, gondola mid-station (1790 m)</name>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.816220" lon="8.396650">
    <name>Engelberg: Titlis Xpress valley station (1000 m)</name>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.979230" lon="9.417040">
    <name>Pizol (Bad Ragaz / Wangs, St. Gallen) [gondola]</name>
    <desc>Pizolhütte 2220 m - top of the Gaffia-Pizolhütte chairlift

    Trails
Seven official MTB tours totalling 5.6 to 35.4 km descend from the Pizol massif on natural alpine tracks and forest roads back to Wangs and Bad Ragaz. The riding is scenic and intermediate, with the 5-Seen-Wanderung panorama as the backdrop. This is trail riding with a view, not a built bike park.

    Getting up / price
Two gondola accesses: Wangs to Furt (Pizolbahnen) or Bad Ragaz to Pardiel, then chairlifts to the high terrain. Bike surcharge: 5 CHF single, 15 CHF / 3 rides, 65 CHF season pass, on top of the passenger ticket.

    Open season
Open from June; closed from October (estimated summer lift window).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00
Estimated hours; check Pizolbahnen summer timetable.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Zurich | Train + bus | ~1h10
Sargans | Bus | ~15 min

    Source: Pizolbahnen.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.959740" lon="8.992060">
    <name>Braunwald (Glarus) [gondola, bike free]</name>
    <desc>Seblengrat 1890 m - top of the Grotzenbüel-Seblengrat chairlift

    Trails
A car-free village above Linthal with four lifts that carry bikes for free. Multiple MTB and e-bike routes traverse the sunny Glarus terrace with views into the Todi massif. The riding is XC and trail on alpine and forest paths, with bike guides available locally.

    Getting up / price
The Braunwaldbahn funicular from Linthal, then the Hüttenberg-Grotzenbüel gondola and Gumen mixed lift to the high terrain. Bike transport is free on all lifts. Pay only the passenger ticket.

    Open season
Open from June; closed from October (estimated summer lift window).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00
Estimated hours; check Sportbahnen Braunwald summer timetable.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Zurich | Train + funicular | ~1h15
Linthal | Funicular | ~7 min

    Source: Braunwald tourism.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.080440" lon="9.290260">
    <name>Flumserberg - BikerBerg (St. Gallen) [35 CHF]</name>
    <desc>Prodalp 1575 m - top of the Prodalp-Express

    Trails
13 km of easy and intermediate BikerTrails above the Walensee, which makes this the friendliest gravity day within an hour of Zurich. BlueSalamander drops from Prodalp, and Red Fox and Red Rock come off the Prodkamm chairlift higher up. Nothing here is trying to frighten you; it is a place to build confidence with a lake view.

    Getting up / price
The 12-seat Prodalp-Express gondola from Tannenheim, plus the Prodkamm chairlift. Biker day ticket 35 CHF, including both lifts and the trails.

    Open season
Open from 23 May; closed from 26 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Zurich | Train + bus | ~1h30
Zurich | Car | ~1h00

    Source: Flumserberg.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
