  <wpt lat="46.508010" lon="9.818530">
    <name>St. Moritz - Corviglia (Engadin) [lift pass, price unverified]</name>
    <desc>Corviglia 2485 m - top of the Signalbahn and the Marguns gondola

    Trails
High, wide and open, with the Engadin lakes below you for the whole descent. Corviglia is the hub: flow trails drop towards St. Moritz and Celerina, and the surrounding valley has one of the densest marked mountain-bike networks in Switzerland once you are willing to pedal between lifts. Not a bike park in the berms-and-tables sense, more a lift-served alpine playground.

    Getting up / price
The Signalbahn from St. Moritz Dorf and the gondola from Celerina to Marguns both carry bikes. Engadin publishes summer tariffs seasonally and we could not confirm a 2026 bike day rate; check the operator.

    Open season
Open from 15 June; closed from 19 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Zurich | Train | ~3h15
Chur | Train | ~2h00

    Source: Engadin St. Moritz.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
