  <wpt lat="46.990820" lon="8.251370">
    <name>Pilatus / Fräkmüntegg (Luzern) [gondola]</name>
    <desc>Fräkmüntegg 1410 m - top of the Kriens gondola

    Trails
Technical natural singletrack descends from Fräkmüntegg and Pilatus Kulm (2014 m, reached by a second cable car) toward Kriens and Alpnach. This is raw Prealp riding, not a shaped bike park: steep forest trails, roots and switchbacks from the Krienseregg mid-station down to the Luzern suburbs. The upper Pilatus Kulm sector is high-alpine and exposed.

    Getting up / price
The gondola from Kriens (Luzern) carries bikes to Fräkmüntegg; the Pilatus Kulm cable car above it may not accept bicycles. Day return from Kriens is about 72 CHF; confirm the current bike surcharge before travelling.

    Open season
Open from May; closed from November (estimated summer gondola window).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:30
Estimated hours; verify Pilatus Bahnen summer schedule and bike carriage policy.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lucerne | Bus + gondola | ~30 min
Zurich | Train + bus + gondola | ~1h15

    Source: Pilatus Bahnen. Confirm bike carriage, trail conditions and lift prices before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.969500" lon="8.637170">
    <name>Stoos - Fronalpstock (Schwyz) [funicular + chairlift]</name>
    <desc>Fronalpstock 1900 m - top of the Mettlen-Fronalpstock chairlift

    Trails
A car-free resort accessible only by the world's steepest funicular, with a network of SuisseMobile mountain-bike routes in a panorama setting above Lake Lucerne. Trails are natural and shared-use, descending from Fronalpstock and Klingenstock (1900 m) back to the Stoos plateau (1300 m) or all the way to the valley. The riding is scenic XC and enduro rather than built park.

    Getting up / price
The Morschach-Stoos cable car or the Schwyz-Stoos funicular (bike surcharge ~5 CHF). From Stoos, chairlifts to Fronalpstock and Klingenstock carry bikes. A combined return from Schwyz is about 44 CHF + bike supplement.

    Open season
Open from June; closed from October (estimated summer lift window).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00
Estimated hours; check the Stoos Bahnen summer timetable.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lucerne | Train + funicular | ~1h
Zurich | Train + funicular | ~1h15

    Source: Stoos tourist office.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.775910" lon="8.269170">
    <name>Melchsee-Frutt (Obwalden) [gondola]</name>
    <desc>Melchsee-Frutt 1925 m - top of the Stöckalp gondola

    Trails
High-alpine XC and enduro riding at 1900-2200 m around Lake Melchsee, with panoramic loops and additional chairlift-served descents from Bonistock (2148 m) and Erzegg (2136 m). Trails are natural mountain paths shared with hikers rather than purpose-built bike trails. The altitude, views and clean air make it a proper summer escape from the lowlands.

    Getting up / price
The Stöckalp-Melchsee-Frutt gondola carries bikes to the high plateau. Additional chairlifts (Cheselen, Jäst, Bettenalp, Erzegg, Bonistock) run higher. Confirm the current bike ticket and lift schedule before travelling.

    Open season
Open from June; closed from mid-October (estimated summer lift window).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00
Estimated hours; check the Melchsee-Frutt summer timetable.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lucerne | Car / bus | ~1h
Stöckalp valley station | Gondola | ~15 min

    Source: Melchsee-Frutt.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.011580" lon="8.789890">
    <name>Hoch-Ybrig (Schwyz) [38 CHF]</name>
    <desc>Seebli 1460 m - top of the Weglosen 3S gondola

    Trails
A 100+ km network of shared mountain paths and natural singletrack across two valleys in the Schwyz Prealps. Trails are well-developed alpine ways rather than dedicated MTB routes, with the Sternen and Spirstock chairlifts adding higher access. This is a scenic trail-riding destination with good lift infrastructure, not a built bike park.

    Getting up / price
The 3S gondola from Weglosen to Seebli, plus chairlifts to Sternen and Spirstock. Summer day pass 38 CHF adult, 10 CHF child (6-16). Bike transport is included or free; no dedicated bike surcharge published.

    Open season
Open from 4 July; closed from 18 October (expected 2026 summer window).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00
Published summer lift window estimate; verify the operator timetable.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Zurich | Car | ~55 min
Winterthur | Car | ~55 min

    Source: Hoch-Ybrig.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.150280" lon="6.685490">
    <name>Les Gets - Chavannes (Portes du Soleil, FR) [38 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Chavannes 1490 m - top of the Chavannes gondola

    Trails
128 km of marked trail on its own, and the gateway to the 650 km Portes du Soleil network next door. The Chavannes side holds most of the bike park - flow lines, jump trails and a well-judged green progression - while Mont Chery across the valley has the steep, rooty World Championship downhill track. As complete a bike-park week as France offers.

    Getting up / price
The Chavannes gondola and Chavannes Express from the village at 1170 m, plus the Mont Chery gondola. A Portes du Soleil day pass is 38 EUR online, 40 EUR at the desk; season 438 EUR. A single Les Gets lift ride is 9.30 EUR.

    Open season
Open from 19 June; closed from 13 September (published 2026 dates). Mont Chery closes 30 August; pre-opening weekends from 22 May.
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Car | ~2h00

    Source: Les Gets.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
