  <wpt lat="46.055470" lon="6.702320">
    <name>Samoens - Grand Massif (FR) [33 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Samoens 1600 - top of the Grand Massif Express

    Trails
The Grand Massif Express climbs almost 900 m out of the valley floor, which gives Samoens some of the longest continuous descents in Haute-Savoie. The bike park itself is moderate rather than extreme, but the pass covers Flaine, Les Carroz and Morillon too, so an enduro day linking four resorts is the real draw.

    Getting up / price
The Grand Massif Express gondola from Samoens at 700 m. A Grand Massif pedestrian and bike day pass is 33 EUR and covers the whole domain; single-resort day passes at Les Carroz and Morillon are 20-21 EUR.

    Open season
Open from 27 June; closed from 31 August (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Car | ~2h15

    Source: Samoens.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.076530" lon="6.721230">
    <name>Samoens: Grand Massif Express valley station (700 m)</name>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.455800" lon="6.919620">
    <name>Tignes (Tarentaise, FR) [20 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Toviere 2695 m - top of the Toviere gondola

    Trails
High-altitude riding at the top of the Tarentaise: the Tignes - Val d'Isere bike area counts 230 km of routes across downhill, enduro and cross-country, most of it above 2000 m and above the trees. Rocky, fast and exposed, with a short season to match. One of the cheapest big lift passes in the French Alps.

    Getting up / price
The Toviere gondola from Tignes le Lac at 2090 m, plus the Palafour and other summer lifts. Bike day pass 20 EUR, six days 80 EUR, season 160 EUR; lifts also included in the My Tignes activity card.

    Open season
Open from 4 July; closed from 30 August (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lausanne | Car | ~3h15
Chambery | Car | ~2h15

    Source: Tignes.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.468240" lon="6.907230">
    <name>Tignes: Toviere gondola base, Tignes le Lac (2090 m)</name>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.925010" lon="6.571110">
    <name>Serre Chevalier (Hautes-Alpes, FR) [28 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Ratier 1895 m - top of the Ratier gondola, Chantemerle

    Trails
A big, sunny, south-facing domain strung along the Guisane valley, with four sectors and enough vertical that the descents to the valley floor go on far longer than you expect. Chantemerle and Villeneuve carry the bike park; the Serre Chevalier cable car above Ratier reaches 2470 m for the high traverses. Larch forest, dry dirt and 300 days of sun a year.

    Getting up / price
The Ratier gondola from Chantemerle at 1360 m; the Casse du Boeuf chairlift at Villeneuve opens first each season. Bike day pass 28 EUR, two non-consecutive days 48.50 EUR, adult season 270.50 EUR.

    Open season
Open from 20 June; closed from 30 August (published 2026 dates). Chantemerle opens 27 June, Briancon and Monetier 4 July.
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Grenoble | Car | ~1h45
Marseille | Car | ~3h00

    Source: Serre Chevalier.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
