  <wpt lat="50.368480" lon="-119.063760">
    <name>SilverStar Bike Park (British Columbia) [84 CAD]</name>
    <desc>Silver Star summit 1885 m - top of the Summit Express gondola

    Trails
Canada's second-largest bike park, and the one riders name when they have had enough of Whistler's crowds. Over 69 km of park trail inside a 139 km network, more than 870 berms, and a spread that runs from mellow green flow to double-black tech. The Comet Six Pack is the biggest mountain-bike lift in the country, 480 m of vertical in under eight minutes. Dry Okanagan dirt, which rides fast.

    Getting up / price
The Summit Express gondola and the Comet Six Pack from the village at 1600 m. Adult day ticket 84 CAD.

    Open season
Open from 21 June; closed from 15 September (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Kelowna | Car | ~1h15
Vancouver | Car | ~4h45

    Source: SilverStar.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
