  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.899860" lon="-119.909240">
    <name>Sun Peaks Bike Park (British Columbia) [82 CAD]</name>
    <desc>Sunburst 1850 m - top of the Sunburst Express

    Trails
Three mountains, high alpine terrain and a park that leans towards long, sustained descents rather than lap-the-jump-line repetition. Sunburst is the gravity hub; the cross-country network above the village is genuinely worth a day of its own. Quieter and cheaper than Whistler, with the same dry interior dirt as SilverStar two hours away.

    Getting up / price
The Sunburst Express chairlift from the village at 1260 m. Adult day ticket 82 CAD at the window, up to 35% less booked online in advance.

    Open season
Open from 20 June; closed from 7 September (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Kamloops | Car | ~50 min
Vancouver | Car | ~4h30

    Source: Sun Peaks.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
