  <wpt lat="49.463860" lon="-115.105800">
    <name>Fernie Alpine Resort (British Columbia) [lift ticket, price unverified]</name>
    <desc>Elk Quad top 1365 m - the bike park's main unload

    Trails
Steep, raw and unmistakably Kootenay: loam, roots, rock rolls and old-growth cedar, on a mountain that gets enough rain to keep the dirt tacky when the Okanagan parks are blown out. The Elk Quad serves the park trails; the Timber Bowl and Great Bear chairs open the bigger terrain above. Not the place to learn, and much loved by people who already know how.

    Getting up / price
The Elk Quad from the resort base at 1065 m, daily 10:00 to 16:00 and until 19:00 on Tuesdays and Thursdays. The resort sells day tickets through its own store; we could not confirm a 2026 adult rate, so check skifernie.com.

    Open season
Open from 25 June; closed from 7 September (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:00
Published hours; Tuesdays and Thursdays run until 19:00.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Calgary | Car | ~3h00
Cranbrook | Car | ~1h15

    Source: Fernie Alpine Resort.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
