  <wpt lat="45.289510" lon="-72.637660">
    <name>Bromont (Quebec) [70-95 CAD, dynamic]</name>
    <desc>Mont Brome 540 m - top of the Express du Village

    Trails
The busiest bike park in Quebec and one of the longest-running in North America, with a ticket that also opens the neighbouring Parc des Sommets network. Only 340 m of vertical, but the trail count and the night-riding operation mean people ride here all season rather than making a pilgrimage. Flow, jump lines and technical Eastern Townships granite in about equal measure.

    Getting up / price
Six lifts serve the mountain from the village at 200 m. Adult single-day tickets are dynamically priced between 70 and 95 CAD - the earlier you book, the cheaper - and an unlimited adult season pass is 699 CAD, taxes extra.

    Open season
Open from 15 May; closed from 26 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Montreal | Car | ~1h00
Sherbrooke | Car | ~45 min

    Source: Bromont.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
