  <wpt lat="36.728350" lon="137.840340">
    <name>Hakuba Iwatake Bike Park (Nagano) [4800 JPY]</name>
    <desc>Iwatake summit 1290 m - top of the Noah gondola

    Trails
The gravity centre of the Hakuba Valley, with the Northern Alps filling the skyline across the valley. Alps Downhill is the signature run: 6.9 km of rolling berms that a confident beginner can ride and an expert can carry real speed down. Kamikaze Downhill is the opposite - steep, rooty, rock-gardened singletrack with a long-standing reputation. A pump track and skills area sit at the base.

    Getting up / price
The Noah gondola lifts riders and bikes from 745 m to the 1290 m summit in about eight minutes. One-day gondola pass 4800 JPY for the bike park.

    Open season
Open from 25 April; closed from 15 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-16:30
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Tokyo | Train + bus | ~3h30
Nagano | Train + bus | ~1h15

    Source: Hakuba Iwatake.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
