  <wpt lat="-36.894370" lon="-71.426980">
    <name>Nevados de Chillan (Nuble, CL) [lift pass, price unverified]</name>
    <desc>El Refugio top 1840 m - the higher of the two bike lifts

    Trails
Seventeen trails on the flank of an active volcano, in araucaria and native forest: ten flow lines that suit a beginner, five fast enduro descents and two cross-country circuits. El Refugio is the newer lift and opens the harder terrain; El Tata covers the park pistes. It hosted the UCI Masters Mountain Bike World Championships in March 2026, on the Aguila downhill course and the Olimpico cross-country loop.

    Getting up / price
Two chairlifts take bikes, El Tata and El Refugio, both from Plaza Tata at 1535 m, where the ticket office, rental and cafe are. The park runs 10:00 to 16:45. Tickets load onto a rechargeable card; we could not confirm a 2026 bike day rate, so check nevadosdechillan.com.

    Open season
Open from 1 December; closed from 30 April (typical window; check the operator and conditions). Southern-hemisphere season.
Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:45
Published operating hours; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Chillan | Car | ~1h30
Santiago | Car | ~6h00

