  <wpt lat="17.221892" lon="-96.580807">
    <name>Oaxaca - Sierra Norte / Ixtepeji (MX) [shuttle, no lift]</name>
    <desc>Santa Catarina Ixtepeji 2355 m - the shuttle village

    Trails
Where enduro started in Mexico, and still the best riding in the country. The Ixtepeji forest, 45 minutes north of Oaxaca City, holds long descents through semi-wet pine and oak between roughly 2800 m and 3240 m on the ridge above, dropping thousands of metres towards the valley. Dry rocky lines, loamy forest lines, and enough of them that operators run multi-day trips without repeating.

    Getting up / price
No lift: pickups shuttle riders to the ridge, which is how essentially all Mexican gravity riding works. The trails cross communal Zapotec land, so go with one of the Oaxaca operators rather than turning up alone - it is also how the communities get paid. Costs are per-tour, not per-day, so no pass price here.

    Open season
Open from 1 November; closed from 15 June (typical window; check the operator and conditions). The summer rains are the off season.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Oaxaca City | Car | ~45 min

    Source: Sierra Norte Expediciones.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="19.191510" lon="-100.113929">
    <name>Valle de Bravo - Monte Alto (MX) [shuttle, no lift]</name>
    <desc>Parque Estatal Monte Alto 2120 m - the main trail area

    Trails
Mexico's best-known mountain-bike town, an hour and a half west of Mexico City above a lake. Monte Alto is the marked and maintained core - pine and oak forest, well signed, views down onto the town - and there are seven distinct riding areas around the valley in total, from beginner loops to steep downhill used for national races.

    Getting up / price
No lift. Local operators run vans up from the town centre and pick you up at the bottom; you can also pedal, since the climb from the lake is only a few hundred metres. Trail access itself is free.

    Open season
Open from 1 November; closed from 1 June (typical window; check the operator and conditions). The summer rains are the off season.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Mexico City | Car | ~2h30
Toluca | Car | ~1h15

    Source: Trailforks Valle de Bravo.
