  <wpt lat="9.960528" lon="-84.531904">
    <name>Buen Camino Bike Park (San Mateo, CR) [25 USD, no lift]</name>
    <desc>San Mateo, Alajuela - access town for the park (pin approximate)

    Trails
A purpose-built 128-hectare bike park in tropical mountain forest an hour west of San Jose, and the most developed thing of its kind in Central America. Graded like a proper park: Viejo Verde as the green, El Patron and Jaguar as blues, Boss and Machete as double blacks, with jumps, wooden bridges and long sections of dense jungle. There is a restaurant and six cabins on site.

    Getting up / price
No lift - you ride up and descend. Bike day pass 25 USD bought on site, hiking 15 USD; full-day bike rental about 130 USD. Open Wednesday to Monday, 08:00 to 16:00, closed Tuesdays. The park sits on Finca Ecologica El Bosque above San Mateo; it has no OpenStreetMap entry, so this pin marks the town rather than the gate.

    Open season
Open from 1 January with no seasonal closure (normally open year-round).
Daily opening hours: 08:00-16:00
Published Wednesday-Monday hours; closed Tuesday.

    Access
