  <wpt lat="46.556330" lon="11.922790">
    <name>Alta Badia - Bike Beats (South Tyrol) [28 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Piz Sorega 1995 m - top of the San Cassiano gondola

    Trails
Five hand-built flow trails through the larch woods under the Sella and the Lavarella, and the most photogenic riding in the Dolomites for the effort involved. Odli is the easy 1.5 km panoramic serpentine, Avena the 2 km blue, Cor the 1.3 km red, with Fle and Mans making up the rest. Northshore sections, rollers and jumps rather than steep raw descents - this is a place to ride all day and enjoy it, not to get scared.

    Getting up / price
Three lifts take bikes: Piz Sorega from San Cassiano at 1545 m, La Fraina and Pralongia. A Moviment daily card is about 28 EUR. The Gravity Card is valid on the Bike Beats lifts. Note that the Mans trail was closed for maintenance when this was compiled.

    Open season
Open from 18 June; closed from 2 October (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Bolzano | Car | ~1h20
Brunico | Car | ~50 min

    Source: Alta Badia Bike Beats.
