  <wpt lat="45.075900" lon="14.157400">
    <name>Bike Park Rabac (HR) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Rabac, Istria - purpose-built coastal trail centre

    Trails
A compact purpose-built network above the Adriatic, part of the wider Maslinica trail system. It mixes easier flow and family trails with rocky technical descents, switchbacks, pump-track features and harder downhill-style lines on dry limestone terrain. The sea views and mild coast climate make it a particularly useful shoulder-season destination, with Bike Center Rabac providing rental, repairs, washing, storage and guided rides.

    Getting up / price
No lift: pedal the climbing roads and connectors or arrange transport through a local operator. Trail access is generally free; rentals and guided services are separate. Rock is sharp and polished in places, so sturdy tyres and protection are sensible.

    Open season
Open from 1 January with no seasonal closure in a typical year. The destination markets year-round cycling; avoid the hottest summer afternoons and check trail conditions after storms.
Daily opening hours: 08:00-18:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Pula | Car | ~50 min
Rijeka | Car | ~1h10

    Sources: Rabac cycling and Bike Center services and Bike Park Rabac overview.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.168900" lon="23.728900">
    <name>Mount Parnitha Enduro (Athens, GR) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Mount Parnitha above Athens - rocky Mediterranean enduro

    Trails
The most established gravity-oriented natural riding area near Athens, with pine and fir forest, exposed limestone, loose rock, fast earth and technical descents between roughly 1000 m and the lower foothills. A representative guided route is about 30 km with 600 m of climbing and roughly 50 percent trail. This is an informal shared-use network rather than a signed park, and route choice matters after fires or forestry work.

    Getting up / price
No bike lift. Pedal from the foothills, self-shuttle by road, or book a guided vehicle-assisted day; one published guided option starts from 85 EUR per person for a group of five, with bike rental extra. Carry offline mapping and yield to walkers.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; Wildfire danger can close the mountain at short notice. Do not ride during official fire restrictions, and avoid wet limestone and peak summer heat.

    Open season
Open from 1 October; closed from 1 June (typical cool-season window, not an official opening calendar). Check fire restrictions and local trail reports.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Athens centre | Car | ~45 min
Athens airport | Car | ~50 min

    Sources: Aegean Trails Parnitha enduro tour and Discover Greece MTB destinations. Seasonal dates are a conservative average.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="41.368400" lon="19.916000">
    <name>Dajti Mountain Enduro (Tirana, AL) [gondola]</name>
    <desc>Fusha e Dajtit above Tirana - natural forest riding with gondola access

    Trails
Albania's most accessible mountain riding zone, with informal routes from the Dajti plateau through beech and pine forest toward Tirana. Expect rough natural paths, rock, roots, steep sections and exceptional views over the capital and Adriatic plain rather than shaped or graded bike-park runs. Formal waymarking and maintenance remain limited, so a guide or strong offline navigation is recommended.

    Getting up / price
Dajti Ekspres reaches the plateau and is reported to carry bikes, giving access without a full road climb. Confirm bicycle acceptance before travelling because operating rules can change. Road shuttles and pedalling are alternatives; there is no dedicated bike patrol or uplift ticket.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; Shared national-park terrain: control speed around walkers, respect closures and do not assume every hiking path permits or suits bikes.

    Open season
Open from 1 March; closed from 1 December (typical riding window). Low trails may be rideable in winter; check gondola operation, rain and snow conditions.
Daily opening hours: 09:00-18:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Tirana centre | Car / bus | ~25 min to gondola
Tirana airport | Car | ~40 min

    Sources: Albanian tourism authority and 2026 Albania cycling guide. Seasonal dates are an average.</desc>
  </wpt>
