    <desc>Gethin Woods above Merthyr Tydfil - the UK's largest gravity trail network

    Trails
More than fifty all-weather trails cover genuine beginner progression, high-speed flow, jumps and steep technical race-style terrain. Kermit provides a long green introduction, while the red, black and pro lines make the park a destination for experienced riders as well.

    Getting up / price
Dedicated vehicles provide booked uplift, or riders can buy pedal and e-bike access. Dynamic session prices were not reliably exposed, so check the official booking calendar.

    Open season
Normally open year-round on scheduled days. Booking availability, storms and trail work can affect individual dates.
Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:30
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Cardiff | Car | ~45 min
Bristol | Car | ~1h30

    Source: official BikePark Wales site; uplift booking is strongly recommended.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.623753" lon="-3.852304">
    <name>Dyfi Bike Park (Wales, UK) [uplift price unverified]</name>
    <desc>Dyfi Forest - big-mountain gravity trails built by the Athertons

    Trails
A 650-acre destination with hand-built red through triple-black trails. Long, fast and technical descents combine natural rock and roots with large jumps and race-scale features. There is no beginner terrain: even the red trails require solid bike-park skills.

Red Bull Hardline
The first Red Bull Hardline was created here in 2014, and the Dyfi Valley remained the original Welsh Hardline venue through its later editions. The invitation-only Hardline race course is separate from the public bike-park trail menu; ride only trails opened by Dyfi Bike Park.

    Getting up / price
Land Rover shuttles provide uplift from the base. Prices and operating days vary through the booking calendar, so reserve directly with the park.

    Open season
Normally open year-round on selected booked days, subject to Welsh mountain weather, events and maintenance closures.
Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:30
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Aberystwyth | Car | ~45 min
Manchester | Car | ~2h30

    Sources: official Dyfi Bike Park history and trail information and Red Bull Hardline series; advance booking required.</desc>
  </wpt>
