  <wpt lat="56.852366" lon="-4.999258">
    <name>Nevis Range (Fort William, UK) [39.85 GBP online]</name>
    <desc>Aonach Mor 650 m gondola station - World Cup downhill above Fort William

    Trails
Three major gondola descents: the legendary orange World Cup track, tight technical black Top Chief and the more approachable Blue Doon. Lower Witches trails add year-round pedal-access riding below the gondola. Highland weather, rocks and sustained vertical make even the easier mountain line demanding. Aonach Mor also hosts MacAvalanche, a mass start race on snow and rough open mountain before riders funnel into the lower trail network.

    Getting up / price
The Mountain Gondola carries riders and bikes in about fifteen minutes. The 2026 adult online multi-trip uplift is 39.85 GBP, or 41.95 GBP at the ticket office.

    Open season
Open from 1 May; closed from 1 October (typical bike-uplift window). Lower trails remain open year-round, while gondola dates and individual descents depend on weather, events and maintenance.
Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:30
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Fort William | Car / bus | ~15 min
Glasgow | Car | ~2h45

    Sources: official Nevis Range 2026 uplift page and MacAvalanche 2026; check the daily mountain report.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="55.656936" lon="-3.182007">
    <name>Glentress 7stanes (Scotland, UK) [no lift, parking fee]</name>
    <desc>Glentress Forest - 75 km of purpose-built Tweed Valley singletrack

    Trails
Scotland's flagship trail centre ranges from green family loops and blue progression trails to long red and black routes. Modern flow finales sit alongside classic rooty and rocky forest singletrack, with enough climbing and distance for full-day rides.

    Getting up / price
No lift: all official routes are pedal-accessed. Trails are free, with all-day parking charged at the visitor centre; bike hire, coaching, showers and food are available.

    Open season
Normally open year-round. Forestry work, storms and repairs regularly divert or close individual sections, so check current notices.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Edinburgh | Car | ~1h00
Edinburgh | Bus | ~1h30

    Source: Forestry and Land Scotland; follow live diversions.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="55.619074" lon="-3.063384">
    <name>Innerleithen and Golfie (Scotland, UK) [optional shuttle]</name>
    <desc>Traquair and Caberston forests - technical Tweed Valley enduro

    Trails
Innerleithen's four formal downhill tracks drop steeply from Plora Rig, while the adjacent Golfie in Caberston Forest is famous for demanding natural enduro trails. Expect roots, mud, rock, steep chutes and limited easy options; this is primarily an expert destination.

    Getting up / price
Pedal and push-up access is always the baseline. Adrenalin Uplift runs a bookable shuttle to the formal downhill hill when available; current prices and dates depend on its calendar.

    Open season
Normally rideable year-round, subject to storm damage, forestry operations, trail maintenance and shuttle availability.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Edinburgh | Car | ~1h10
Glentress | Car | ~15 min

    Source: Forestry and Land Scotland; clean bikes to limit forest disease and obey closures.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.260000" lon="16.814000">
    <name>Bike Park Czarna Gora (PL) [119 PLN weekdays]</name>
    <desc>Czarna Gora 1205 m - one of Poland's largest lift-served parks

    Trails
Nineteen maintained trails cover beginner flow, skills zones, freeride, enduro and advanced downhill. The Kids and Skills arenas make progression unusually accessible, while the steeper race lines provide serious rock, roots and technical features.

    Getting up / price
The Luxtorpeda chairlift and Efka lift carry bikes. The published 2026 adult weekday day pass is 119 PLN; weekend pricing can be higher.

    Open season
Open from 1 May; closed from 1 November (typical 2026 lift window; reduced schedules and maintenance closures apply).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Wroclaw | Car | ~2h00
Prague | Car | ~3h00

    Source: official Bike Park Czarna Gora site; check lift status.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.575566" lon="16.658923">
    <name>Enduro Trails Srebrna Gora (PL) [shuttle price unverified]</name>
    <desc>Srebrna Gora - shuttle-assisted Lower Silesian enduro

    Trails
Long purpose-built and natural descents use roughly 330 m of vertical around the historic fortress. Lines range from flowing intermediate riding to steep technical enduro with rock, roots and tight forest sections; SGR Line is the signature expert descent.

    Getting up / price
Commercial vans and trailers provide booked uplift, with pedalling also possible. Current shuttle prices vary by package and were not reliably published in the sources checked.

    Open season
Open from 1 April; closed from 1 December (typical riding and shuttle window; check booking availability).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Wroclaw | Car | ~1h30
Prague | Car | ~3h00

    Sources: Srebrna Gora trail information and NS Bikeparks; reserve uplift in advance.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.759856" lon="19.001475">
    <name>Enduro Trails Bielsko-Biala (PL) [no lift, free trails]</name>
    <desc>Blonia trail centre - Poland's best-known pedal-access enduro network

    Trails
A large signed network on the wooded hills above Bielsko-Biala, combining machine-built flow with technical natural enduro. Climbing trails link green and blue progression lines to red and black descents; the area hosted Enduro World Cup racing.

    Getting up / price
No lift at the main Blonia network: climb the signed uphill trails. Trail access is free, with rentals, coaching and services available at the base.

    Open season
Open from 1 April; closed from 1 December (typical window). Respect wet-weather, forestry and event closures.
Daily opening hours: 08:00-18:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Katowice | Car / train | ~1h15
Krakow | Car | ~1h30

    Source: official Enduro Trails site; check current trail status.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.717046" lon="20.159665">
    <name>Bike Park Kasina (PL) [169 PLN]</name>
    <desc>Snieznica above Kasina Wielka - compact lift-served gravity park

    Trails
A well-established Polish park with flow, jump and downhill lines packed into a compact hill. Easier shaped trails support progression, while rooty forest tracks and steeper technical variants suit advanced riders.

    Getting up / price
A high-speed chairlift carries bikes. The published 2026 regular adult day ticket is 169 PLN, or 149 PLN with the phone-sticker pass.

    Open season
Open from 1 May; closed from 1 November (typical operating window; check weekday and shoulder-season schedules).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
