  <wpt lat="48.037592" lon="6.972643">
    <name>La Bresse-Hohneck Bike Park (Vosges, FR) [31 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Vologne Express summit above La Bresse - rocky Vosges DH and freeride

    Trails
Ten maintained descents split between six technical DH tracks and four freeride lines. A green trail gives newcomers a route into the park, while the red and black lines are known for rough rock, roots, braking bumps and demanding race-style riding.

    Getting up / price
The Vologne Express chairlift carries bikes. The published 2026 adult day pass is 31 EUR; equipment rental and instruction are available at the resort.

    Open season
Open from 1 May; closed from 21 September (published 2026 dates). Daily operation runs from 4 July through 30 August, with a reduced schedule outside it.
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Colmar | Car | ~1h00
Nancy | Car | ~1h45

    Source: official La Bresse Bike Park page; check trail status.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.368125" lon="4.528009">
    <name>Pilat Enduro Trails (near Lyon, FR) [no lift, free trails]</name>
    <desc>Croix de Chaubouret above Saint-Etienne - official natural enduro network

    Trails
Six official enduro itineraries cross the varied Pilat massif, from shorter intermediate descents to the 18.6 km Col du Gratteau route with roughly 1100 m of climbing. These are shared natural paths rather than closed bike-park tracks, combining forest singletrack, rock, roots and linking climbs.

    Getting up / price
No lift and no mandatory trail fee. Ride the routes as pedal-powered itineraries or arrange your own point-to-point transport; riders must yield to walkers.

    Open season
Open from 1 March; closed from 1 December (typical riding window). Snow, freeze-thaw, storms and forestry work can shorten the season.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Saint-Etienne | Car | ~25 min
Lyon | Car | ~1h10

    Source: official Pilat enduro route page; shared paths are not downhill-only tracks.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.803367" lon="6.097538">
    <name>Semnoz Bike Park (Annecy, FR) [17.50 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Semnoz above Lake Annecy - compact new Télémix-served park

    Trails
Four dedicated descents provide unusually clear progression close to Annecy: one family green, one more technical blue and two red trails with shaped turns, jumps and modules. It is a compact park rather than a full holiday domain, but its accessibility makes it a valuable local gravity spot.

    Getting up / price
The Télémix carries bikes to the trail starts. The published 2026 adult day pass is 17.50 EUR, or 14.50 EUR for four consecutive hours.

    Open season
Open from 20 June; closed from 21 September (published 2026 dates). Daily operation runs from 4 July through 30 August; June and September have selected weekend dates.
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Annecy | Car / summer bus | ~35 min
Lausanne | Car | ~1h35

    Source: official Semnoz Bike Park page; check operating dates.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.958840" lon="6.455653">
    <name>Le Grand-Bornand MTB (Aravis, FR) [20 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Rosay and Lachat above Le Grand-Bornand - lift-assisted Aravis trail riding

    Trails
More than 178 km across sixteen marked routes combine high alpine tracks, natural singletrack, cross-country loops and long descents into the village. The riding is less shaped than a dedicated DH park; the Grand Tour and Enduro du Grand-Bo are the notable sportier options.

    Getting up / price
The Rosay gondola and Lachat chairlift provide bike access to the upper network. The published 2026 adult day pass covering both lifts is 20 EUR.

    Open season
Open from 27 June; closed from 7 September (published 2026 span, including preview and closing weekends). Core daily operation runs from 4 July through 29 August.
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Annecy | Car | ~45 min
Lausanne | Car | ~1h35

    Source: official 2026 summer guide; check which lift serves your route.</desc>
  </wpt>
