  <wpt lat="37.628151" lon="128.677729">
    <name>Mona YongPyong MTB Park (Pyeongchang, KR) [gondola, public price unverified]</name>
    <desc>Balwangsan at Mona YongPyong - South Korea's 2026 UCI World Cup gravity venue

    Trails
Purpose-built downhill and cross-country race terrain on the steep forested slopes of Balwangsan. Mona YongPyong hosted Asia's first UCI Mountain Bike World Series round in May 2026, with a full downhill course, technical natural sections and a dedicated finish bowl. This is serious race terrain rather than a broad beginner holiday network.

    Getting up / price
The resort gondola carried bikes from the main venue to the downhill start and the Rainbow chairlift returned accredited riders during the 2026 World Cup. A normal public bike-uplift price and calendar were not verified, so contact the resort before travelling outside an announced MTB event.

    Open season
Open from 1 May; closed from 1 October (estimated snow-free riding window). Public trail and uplift access may be limited to scheduled events even inside this period.
Daily opening hours: 08:30-16:30
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Seoul | Car / intercity bus | ~2h30
Gangneung | Car | ~45 min

    Sources: 2026 UCI event guide and official Mona YongPyong site; confirm public MTB access.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="35.433435" lon="126.738246">
    <name>Gochang MTB Park (Jeonbuk, KR) [no public uplift verified]</name>
    <desc>Bangjangsan foothills at Gochang - one of South Korea's established downhill parks

    Trails
A purpose-built mountain-bike park used for Korean downhill and cross-country riding, with steep forest race lines, rock, roots and technical features. The terrain is best suited to experienced riders; inspect features and current course conditions before committing.

    Getting up / price
No dependable public lift or shuttle service was verified. Plan to pedal or push unless a race or local organizer announces vehicle uplift. No current mandatory access price was published.

    Open season
Open from 1 March; closed from 1 December (typical regional riding window). The official listed hours are 09:00-17:00 and the facility is closed on Mondays; weather or events can change access.
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Published hours; closed Monday.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Gwangju | Car | ~55 min
Jeonju | Car | ~1h15

    Source: official Gochang tourism listing; verify course status locally.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="35.184700" lon="129.044800">
    <name>Baegyangsan MTB Trails (Busan, KR) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Baegyangsan above central Busan - natural urban mountain-bike network

    Trails
A dense mix of forest roads and natural singletrack with sustained climbing, rooty enduro descents and steeper downhill options. Local routes cover beginner, intermediate and advanced riding, but these are shared mountain paths rather than signed, bike-only park tracks. Start from the Busan Children's Grand Park side for convenient access.

    Getting up / price
No lift and no mandatory trail fee: pedal the forest-road climbs and connect the natural descents. Yield to walkers, avoid busy hiking periods and respect any temporary closures.

    Open season
Open year-round. Heavy summer rain, typhoons, ice and freeze-thaw conditions can make the steep natural trails unsuitable; avoid riding when the surface is saturated.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Central Busan | Bike / metro and bike | ~30 min

    Sources: Visit Busan mountain guide and Busan Geopark; trails are shared and unsigned for MTB.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="37.563025" lon="126.885155">
    <name>Nanji Hangang Extreme Bike Park (Seoul, KR) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Nanji Hangang Park - compact beginner MTB skills course in Seoul

    Trails
South Korea's first flat-site MTB practice course recreates small mountain contours and slopes in a 5,425 square metre facility. Its 450 m circuit is designed for beginner and intermediate riders to practise bike handling safely. It is a useful city session spot, not a destination downhill park.

    Getting up / price
No lift is needed on the compact circuit. No current admission charge was published; helmets and suitable protective equipment are required.

    Open season
Open year-round. Published hours are 09:00-18:00 in summer and 09:00-16:00 in winter; severe weather or maintenance can close the course.
Daily opening hours: 09:00-18:00
Published summer hours; winter closes at 16:00.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Central Seoul | Bike / metro and bike | ~35 min

    Source: Korea Tourism Organization facility listing.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="5.166000" lon="-75.518000">
    <name>Manizales / Neira Coffee Trails (CO) [shuttle, price unverified]</name>
    <desc>Neira and the cloud-forest ridges above Manizales

    Trails
World-class natural enduro in Colombia's coffee country: long, raw descents mix loam, slick roots, rock, tight jungle turns and plantation paths. The area has hosted Enduro World Series racing, but it is a riding zone rather than a signed bike park; a local guide is strongly recommended.

    Getting up / price
Commercial guides use 4x4 or traditional chiva-style road shuttles. There is no public lift or standard day-pass price, and trail access can cross private farms.

    Open season
Open year-round; December-March and July-August are usually drier. Avoid saturated trails and confirm landslide and private-land access locally.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Manizales | Guide shuttle | ~35 min to Neira

    Sources: Colombia Travel: Trails del Cafe and Colombia MTB.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="6.210000" lon="-75.502000">
    <name>Santa Elena / Medellin Enduro (CO) [shuttle, price unverified]</name>
    <desc>Santa Elena plateau above Medellin - informal gravity network

    Trails
Pine and cloud-forest singletrack descends from the cool plateau toward the Aburra valley, ranging from flowing local lines to steep, rooty and technical enduro. Routes are unsigned, change frequently and share land with walkers and farmers.

    Getting up / price
Use a local 4x4 shuttle, guide, or pedal the roads from Santa Elena. The Arvi Metrocable is useful for visiting the plateau, but bicycle carriage and direct access to gravity trails must be confirmed before relying on it.

    Open season
Open year-round; January-February and July-August are normally driest. Do not ride saturated cloud-forest trails.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Medellin centre | Car / local bus | ~45 min

    Sources: official Medellin tourism guide and Medellin municipality. Ride with local knowledge.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="6.555000" lon="-73.133000">
    <name>San Gil / Chicamocha Mule Trails (CO) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>San Gil and Chicamocha Canyon - rocky backcountry enduro

    Trails
Historic mule tracks, dry canyon paths and rough mountain roads create long, rocky adventure rides around San Gil and the Chicamocha rim. This is exposed backcountry riding, not a maintained trail centre; route-finding, heat and water management matter more than bike-park features.

    Getting up / price
No bike lift. Pedal point-to-point, arrange a local vehicle, or book a guide. Confirm access across villages and private land.

    Open season
Open year-round; December-March is typically driest. Avoid the hottest part of the day and check storm conditions in the canyon.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Bucaramanga | Car / bus | ~2h30

    Indicative regional adventure-riding pin; use a local guide and verify the chosen route.

    Source: Colombia Travel.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-22.735000" lon="-45.592000">
    <name>Zoom Bike Park (Campos do Jordao, BR) [price unverified]</name>
    <desc>Campos do Jordao - maintained Mantiqueira trail centre

    Trails
A purpose-built, signed network for XC, all-mountain and enduro, with progression-friendly singletrack, technical lines and e-MTB-suitable climbing. The park is built and maintained specifically for mountain bikes rather than being an informal forest network.

    Getting up / price
No lift was verified: climb under your own power. Current admission, booking and wet-weather status must be checked with the operator.

    Open season
Normally rideable year-round, with rain closures possible.
Daily opening hours: 08:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule and rain closures.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Sao Paulo | Car | ~2h45

    Source: official Zoom Bike Park.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-26.740000" lon="-49.176000">
    <name>Pomeranos DH Trails (Pomerode, BR) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Pomerode hills - Santa Catarina downhill race terrain

    Trails
Steep subtropical forest descents used by the established Pomeranos downhill scene, with roots, red dirt, chutes and race-built technical sections. This is not confirmed as a continuously operated commercial park, so expect local trails rather than a staffed facility.

    Getting up / price
No public lift or standard shuttle was verified. Pedal or arrange access with local riders, and confirm landowner permission before riding.

    Open season
Open year-round when dry; avoid the clay trails after heavy rain.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Blumenau | Car | ~45 min

    Source: Santa Catarina Cycling Federation, which lists Pomeranos downhill events in Pomerode. Confirm current local access.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-20.245000" lon="-46.365000">
    <name>Serra da Canastra Adventure MTB (Minas Gerais, BR) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Sao Roque de Minas gateway - high-plateau adventure riding

    Trails
Long red-dirt roads, rocky tracks, granite slabs and rural connectors cross the Canastra plateau and its waterfall country. The best riding is XC and backcountry trail exploration rather than gravity laps; carry navigation, water and repair equipment.

    Getting up / price
No lift. Pedal point-to-point or arrange a 4x4 support vehicle. National-park entry rules and permitted cycling routes must be checked before departure.

    Open season
Best from May to September in the dry season; summer storms can make river crossings and clay roads unsafe.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Belo Horizonte | Car | ~5h30

    Sources: Brazil Ministry of Tourism and Delfinopolis tourism. Verify protected-area rules.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="14.680256" lon="121.165301">
    <name>Timberland Mountain Bike Park (Rizal, PH) [250-550 PHP]</name>
    <desc>Timberland Heights, San Mateo - purpose-built trail park

    Trails
A patrolled, colour-graded network from beginner flow to expert gravity, with berms, rollers, tabletops, bridges and rollable drops. Expect climbing between descents because there is no uplift.

    Getting up / price
Pedal access. Published passes are 250 PHP weekdays and 550 PHP weekends and holidays, plus the operator's current insurance or registration requirements.

    Open season
Open year-round with a reduced wet-season schedule.
Daily opening hours: 07:00-16:00
Published hours; Wednesday-Sunday in the dry season and Thursday-Sunday in the wet season.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Metro Manila | Car | ~1h15

    Source: official Timberland rider information.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="14.068781" lon="120.856839">
    <name>Twin Lakes MTB Trail (Tagaytay, PH) [access status unverified]</name>
    <desc>Twin Lakes estate above Taal - compact scenic trail

    Trails
A 2.5 km off-road loop was built with fast descents, berms, off-camber turns, switchbacks, short climbs and views toward Taal Lake. It was designed for mixed abilities, but current maintenance and public access could not be confirmed from a recent operator page.

    Getting up / price
No lift; pedal the loop. Confirm at the estate before travelling specifically to ride.

    Open season
Potentially year-round when open and dry; avoid typhoon and saturated conditions.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Metro Manila | Car | ~2h

    Source: BusinessWorld trail report. Current status is unverified.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="14.705000" lon="121.151000">
    <name>Mount Maarat / Patiis Trails (Rizal, PH) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Mount Maarat above San Mateo - raw local enduro

    Trails
A long-established local network of brutally steep climbs and loose, rooty jungle descents, including the notorious Shotgun area. Lines are informal and technical rather than marked park trails, and land access can change.

    Getting up / price
No formal lift. Pedal, arrange a local pickup, and ride with people who know current entrances and private-land restrictions.

    Open season
Year-round in principle, but the dry months from November-May are more reliable. Avoid heavy rain and typhoon periods.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Metro Manila | Car | ~1h15

    Sources: Rizal's established Maarat riding area and local trail reports; access is informal and must be confirmed locally.

    Source: Trailforks San Mateo.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-6.786000" lon="107.651000">
    <name>Cikole Gravity Trails (Lembang, ID) [shuttle, price unverified]</name>
    <desc>Cikole pine forest above Bandung - established gravity zone

    Trails
Deep volcanic soil, pine-forest loam, roots and race-built downhill lines make Cikole one of Indonesia's best-known gravity areas. Expect a mix of raw DH, freeride features and locally shaped flow rather than a single unified resort trail map.

    Getting up / price
Local vehicle uplift and riding packages are available around the Cikole recreation area; there is no verified fixed public lift pass. Arrange uplift and guide details before arrival.

    Open season
Open year-round, best in the drier May-October period.
Daily opening hours: 08:00-17:00
Typical area estimate; confirm with the selected uplift or trail operator.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Bandung | Car | ~1h15

    Sources: Cikole's established MTB riding area and Indonesia Travel for the Cikole setting. Confirm the active trail operator.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-7.584000" lon="110.447000">
    <name>Klangon Merapi DH (Yogyakarta, ID) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Klangon Hill on Mount Merapi - volcanic downhill track

    Trails
A recognised downhill competition venue at roughly 1,100 m, with fast, technical dirt and volcanic surfaces under a dramatic view of active Mount Merapi. It is a compact local track, not a large lift-served resort.

    Getting up / price
No public uplift was verified; push or pedal and ask locally about event-day vehicle access. A small general tourism or maintenance fee may apply.

    Open season
Open year-round subject to rain and volcanic exclusion zones.
Daily opening hours: 06:00-18:00
Typical daylight estimate; check weather and volcanic closures locally.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Yogyakarta | Car | ~1h

    Source: Yogyakarta Tourism Portal. Obey all Merapi safety closures.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.242000" lon="115.375000">
    <name>Kintamani / Mount Batur MTB (Bali, ID) [guided shuttle]</name>
    <desc>Kintamani crater rim - volcanic adventure descents

    Trails
Routes start around 1,500 m above the Batur caldera and descend on volcanic sand, dirt tracks, village lanes and tropical singletrack. Guided options range from easy scenic downhill tours to much rougher enduro-style lines toward Tianyar or the lower villages.

    Getting up / price
Commercial tours provide vehicle transfer to Kintamani; no bike lift. Choose an MTB-specific operator because many advertised cycling tours use easy roads rather than technical trails.

    Open season
Best from April-October; wet-season storms make volcanic surfaces and jungle sections unpredictable.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Ubud | Tour shuttle | ~1h15

    Sources: Visit Bali MTB routes and Indonesia Travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="1.030000" lon="104.057000">
    <name>Mangsang Bike Park (Batam, ID) [uplift price unverified]</name>
    <desc>Bukit Mangsang, Batam - downhill and enduro race park

    Trails
A gravity-focused local park with downhill, enduro and XC competition tracks, including steep race sections and a substantial rock garden. It hosted Indonesian national-level MTB competition and draws riders from Singapore and Malaysia.

    Getting up / price
Local packages use vehicle uplift, but no current walk-up schedule or price was verified. Contact the park before taking the ferry with a bike.

    Open season
Open year-round subject to tropical rain and events.
Daily opening hours: 08:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; arrange current access and uplift before arrival.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Batam Centre | Car | ~35 min
Singapore | Ferry + car | ~2h30

    Sources: Batam sports authority and ANTARA.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="3.143500" lon="101.638500">
    <name>Bukit Kiara Trails (Kuala Lumpur, MY) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Bukit Kiara - volunteer-maintained urban jungle network

    Trails
A dense network of roughly 90 named trails, from approachable loops to root-heavy technical all-mountain and downhill lines such as the harder local classics. Trails were built and maintained by riders but are intentionally shared with hikers and runners.

    Getting up / price
Free pedal access; no lift. Climb the tarmac spine or trail connectors, yield to every non-rider and never build or modify lines without local approval.

    Open season
Open year-round, but do not ride during or immediately after tropical downpours.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Central Kuala Lumpur | Car / metro and bike | ~25 min

    Sources: Friends of Bukit Kiara and TRAKS Malaysia.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="6.000000" lon="116.575000">
    <name>Mount Kinabalu Foothills Adventure MTB (Sabah, MY) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <desc>Kundasang and the Crocker Range foothills - Borneo adventure riding

    Trails
Highland farm roads, village tracks and rainforest connectors offer scenic XC and guided adventure riding beneath Mount Kinabalu. This is not a formal bike park, and national-park hiking trails must not be assumed legal for bicycles.

    Getting up / price
No lift. Use a local cycling operator for vehicle support, permission and a legal route; do not enter protected footpaths without approval.

    Open season
Rideable year-round, with February-April usually drier. Tropical storms and mud can close or damage routes quickly.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Kota Kinabalu | Guide vehicle | ~2h

    Indicative regional adventure-riding pin. Confirm a permitted route with a Sabah operator and protected-area authorities.

    Source: Sabah Tourism.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="1.372000" lon="103.776000">
    <name>Chestnut Nature Park MTB Trails (Singapore) [no lift, free]</name>
    <desc>Chestnut Nature Park - purpose-built urban singletrack

    Trails
Singapore's largest nature park separates designated MTB and hiking routes, with rolling singletrack, berms, rock features and mixed-difficulty loops in an 81 ha forest setting. Ride only the marked MTB trails.

    Getting up / price
Free pedal access; no lift. Protect the trail surface by staying away in heavy rain and obey NParks closures.

    Open season
Open year-round.
Daily opening hours: 07:00-19:00
Published NParks opening hours; temporary weather closures may apply.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Central Singapore | Metro/bus + bike | ~45 min

    Source: Singapore NParks.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="1.349000" lon="103.776500">
    <name>Bukit Timah MTB Trail (Singapore) [no lift, free]</name>
    <desc>Dairy Farm / Bukit Timah - Singapore's oldest technical MTB loop

    Trails
A 7 km intermediate-to-advanced designated circuit with fast descents, rock gardens, drops, blind corners and technical climbs. Twenty-three named sections and multiple exits allow riders to shorten the loop.

    Getting up / price
Free pedal access; no lift. Bicycles must remain on the designated MTB trail and riders should follow NParks nature-reserve rules.

    Open season
Open year-round when conditions allow.
Daily opening hours: 07:00-19:00
Typical nature-reserve hours estimate; check NParks notices.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Central Singapore | Metro/bus + bike | ~40 min

    Source: Singapore NParks MTB guide.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="1.405000" lon="103.958000">
    <name>Ketam Mountain Bike Park (Pulau Ubin, SG) [no lift, free]</name>
    <desc>Ketam Quarry, Pulau Ubin - international-standard XC park

    Trails
Ten kilometres of purpose-built tracks around a former quarry, graded from blue square through black and double black. Expect narrow low-grip trail, long stepped climbs, drops, sharp corners and steep technical obstacles rather than uplifted downhill.

    Getting up / price
Free pedal access; no lift. Reach Pulau Ubin by bumboat from Changi Point, then ride from the village. Boat space and bicycle charges vary.

    Open season
Open year-round in daylight, subject to ferry service, rain and NParks closures.
Daily opening hours: 07:00-19:00
Daylight estimate; ferry service and NParks closures control practical access.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Central Singapore | Bus/taxi + bumboat + bike | ~1h30

    Source: Singapore NParks Pulau Ubin cycling guide.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="36.049000" lon="51.417000">
    <name>Dizin / Shemshak Alborz Enduro (IR) [no verified bike lift]</name>
    <desc>Gardaneh Dizin and Shemshak - high-Alborz alpine riding

    Trails
Loose, rocky ski-area roads, ridge tracks and natural paths can produce descents exceeding 1,000 m of vertical in dry, exposed alpine terrain. This is informal backcountry enduro, not a maintained summer bike park.

    Getting up / price
Summer bicycle uplift at Dizin or Shemshak could not be verified. Use a local guide and road shuttle or pedal; do not assume winter lifts carry bikes.

    Open season
Best from June-October after snowmelt. Afternoon storms, altitude and exposure require conservative planning.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Tehran | Car / guide shuttle | ~2h30

    Source: Dizin Pass cycling guide. MTB access is informal and must be verified locally.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="35.817500" lon="51.409000">
    <name>Mount Tochal / Tehran Foothills (IR) [gondola bike access unverified]</name>
    <desc>Tochal above Tehran - huge vertical and technical foothill paths

    Trails
The Alborz rises directly from the city to almost 4,000 m. Rough natural paths around Darakeh and the mid-mountain stations offer rocky, exposed descending, but they are shared hiking terrain rather than sanctioned bike-park runs.

    Getting up / price
The Tochal Telecabin reaches high stations, but current bicycle carriage could not be confirmed. Ask the operator before relying on it; road shuttle and pedalling are safer planning assumptions.

    Open season
Lower foothills are broadly year-round; high routes are normally June-October.
Daily opening hours: 07:30-15:00
Typical gondola estimate; confirm current operation and bicycle acceptance.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Central Tehran | Car / taxi | ~35 min

    Source: Tochal Complex gondola infrastructure; confirm bicycle rules and stay off pedestrian-only paths.

    Source: Tochal.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="36.260000" lon="52.930000">
    <name>Lafur / Mazandaran Forest MTB (IR) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <desc>Lafur Forest - Hyrcanian forest adventure riding

    Trails
Dense beech forest, loamy village tracks, steep mountain roads and wet roots offer a green contrast to Iran's dry southern Alborz. There is no signed trail centre, and forest protection, land access and navigation require local knowledge.

    Getting up / price
No lift. Arrange a guide and vehicle support from Mazandaran; use only permitted roads and tracks.

    Open season
Best from April-June and September-November. Avoid saturated trails, snow and peak summer humidity.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Tehran | Car | ~4h

    Source: Visit Iran: Lafur Forest. This is a regional adventure pin, not a marked MTB park.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="35.900000" lon="52.050000">
    <name>Lar National Park / Damavand MTB (IR) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <desc>Lar Valley beneath Mount Damavand - high-altitude expedition MTB

    Trails
A serious point-to-point backcountry ride across alpine plateau, riverbeds, dirt tracks and high passes beneath Iran's 5,610 m volcano. Commercial itineraries rate it highly demanding and normally take several days.

    Getting up / price
No lift. Guided trips use support vehicles and camps; permits and protected-area access must be arranged in advance.

    Open season
Open from late May through August in a typical year; snow, river levels and conservation closures control access.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Tehran | Guide vehicle | ~2h to western approach

    Sources: Lar Plain MTB itinerary and Adventure Iran trip report.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="40.904000" lon="115.455000">
    <name>Thaiwoo Bike Park (Chongli, CN) [gondola price unverified]</name>
    <desc>Thaiwoo Ski Town - China's flagship lift-served bike park

    Trails
Purpose-built summer MTB terrain with gondola-served flow, jumps, pump-track facilities and technical downhill on the Olympic-region mountains. The operator actively lists mountain biking among its summer sports.

    Getting up / price
Summer gondola uplift is offered, but a current public bike-pass price was not reliably available in English. Confirm ticketing and trail status directly.

    Open season
Open from June; closed from October (typical Chongli bike season).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical summer estimate; check the official daily schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Beijing | Fast train + taxi | ~2h

    Source: official Thaiwoo summer activities.</desc>
