  <wpt lat="22.565000" lon="114.191000">
    <name>Shenzhen Wutong Mountain MTB Trails (CN) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Technical singletrack on Shenzhen's highest peak

    Trails
Mapped mountain-bike lines on Wutong Mountain (944 m) and surrounding hills include graded singletrack from easy blue (Kunpeng Path) to double-black extreme (Extreme Wutong, mtb:scale 6). The Yantian coastal hills add red-grade speed tracks and enduro lines. The Dayun XC loop (2.4 km) near Longgang is the only purpose-built MTB track in the city.

    Getting up / price
No lift. Pedal up or use local shuttle arrangements. Sightseeing gondolas at OCT East and Qiushuishan do not carry bikes.

    Open season
Best October-April. Summer brings extreme heat (35 C+), monsoon rain and typhoon risk.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Central Shenzhen | Metro + bike | ~40 min to Wutong trailhead

    Most trails are unofficial and ride at your own risk; Wutong Mountain's main road formally bans cycling. Verify current access and local conditions before riding.

    Source: OpenStreetMap (30+ mtb-tagged ways, ODbL). Trail access and legality can change; verify before travel.</desc>
