    <desc>Guided tropical trail riding between coast and rainforest

    Trails
Local routes around Sainte-Rose combine sugar-cane tracks, mangrove edges, riverbeds, tropical forest and steeper natural singletrack. The best connections are deliberately not published on standard maps, making this a guided riding zone rather than a signed trail centre.

    Getting up / price
No lift. VELOC offers mountain-bike rental, delivery and local route advice or accompaniment from Sainte-Rose. Confirm the selected route, difficulty and price directly.

    Open season
Guiding and rental are listed year-round in 2026; December-May usually offers drier riding. Routes can close after storms, flooding or forestry damage.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Pointe-a-Pitre | Car | ~35 min
Deshaies | Car | ~30 min

    Sources: Guadeloupe Islands tourism listing and VELOC.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="43.128000" lon="77.080200">
    <name>Shymbulak Bike Park (Almaty, KZ) [uplift status unverified]</name>
    <desc>High-altitude resort terrain above Almaty

    Trails
Shymbulak's published resort rules define a downhill bike park with purpose-built natural and artificial features, using the steep ski terrain between roughly 2,200 and 3,180 m. However, the official 2026 summer programme does not currently list public MTB operation, so trail maintenance and access must be confirmed before travel.

    Getting up / price
The Medeu-Shymbulak gondola and upper lifts operate for summer visitors, but 2026 bicycle carriage, bike-park uplift and prices are unverified. Do not assume a sightseeing ticket includes a bicycle.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; Current bike-park operation is unverified. Contact Shymbulak before planning a riding day.

    Open season
Potential summer operation from June through September; snow, maintenance and national-park restrictions apply.
Daily opening hours: 09:00-18:00
Summer resort estimate only; bicycle uplift and bike-park operation must be confirmed.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Central Almaty | Bus/taxi + gondola | ~45 min

    Sources: official resort overview and the published resort rules.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="43.158000" lon="76.976000">
    <name>Kok-Zhailau MTB (Almaty, KZ) [shared trails, no lift]</name>
    <desc>Alpine plateau and ridge riding directly above Almaty

    Trails
Rocky forest tracks climb from the city edge to the Kok-Zhailau plateau around 2,000-2,200 m. Beginner outings turn around on the plateau; experienced riders can continue toward the meteorological station or exposed ridge terrain. These are busy shared mountain trails, not a bike park.

    Getting up / price
No lift. Pedal from Prosveshchenets or the Medeu side, or book a local guided e-MTB outing. Give way to hikers and horses, especially on summer weekends.

    Open season
Best May-October. Snow, spring mud, thunderstorms and national-park closures affect the higher route.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Central Almaty | Bike / bus + bike | ~30 min to trailhead

    Source: local Kok-Zhailau cycling guide. Confirm permitted routes locally.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="32.316000" lon="77.156700">
    <name>Manali / Solang Valley MTB (Himachal Pradesh, IN) [shuttle, no lift]</name>
    <desc>India's best-known Himalayan gravity base

    Trails
Steep pine-forest singletrack, village paths and rough alpine tracks descend around Solang, Old Manali and the surrounding Kullu mountains. Terrain ranges from guided cross-country to technical enduro and downhill; it is a developing regional network rather than a signed bike park.

    Getting up / price
No verified public bike lift. Local operators arrange 4x4 shuttles, guiding and occasional specialist helibiking, all of which must be booked and checked independently. The government has also planned dedicated Manali and Solang cycling trails, but completion status varies.

    Open season
Best April-June and September-November. Monsoon rain, winter snow, landslides and heavy Solang road traffic can prevent riding.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Manali | Bike / shuttle | ~35 min to Solang
Kullu airport | Car | ~1h30

    Source: Himachal Pradesh mountain-bike trail planning document. Use a current local MTB operator.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="34.278300" lon="77.604600">
    <name>Khardung La / Nubra MTB (Ladakh, IN) [vehicle drop, no lift]</name>
    <desc>Extreme-altitude descent from one of Ladakh's great passes

    Trails
The classic objective is a supported ride from the Khardung La road pass into the Indus or Nubra side, combining a very long high-altitude road descent with optional rough tracks and village routes. It is an expedition ride, not continuous singletrack or a bike park.

    Getting up / price
No lift. Use a licensed local guide and support vehicle from Leh. Current road permits, checkpoints and route restrictions must be verified; independent foreign travel rules can change.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; The pass is above 5,300 m. Acclimatize in Leh first and treat altitude illness, cold, traffic and remote rescue as serious hazards.

    Open season
Usually May-September, entirely dependent on snow clearance, road status and military or civil restrictions.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Leh | Guide vehicle | ~2h to pass

    Source: District Leh adventure tourism guide, which lists Khardung La and Nubra among its mountain-bike areas.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="27.236000" lon="88.422800">
    <name>Temi / South Sikkim MTB (IN) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <desc>Eastern Himalayan riding through tea, forest and mountain villages

    Trails
The Temi and Ravangla area provides steep jeep tracks, tea-garden lanes, forest paths and long mountain-road links beneath views toward Kanchenjunga. Sikkim promotes multiple mountain-bike routes and a state MTB tour, but this remains guided regional riding rather than a formal trail centre.

    Getting up / price
No lift. Arrange rental, permits, guiding and vehicle support in Gangtok or through Sikkim Tourism. Do not enter tea estates, protected forests or village land without permission.

    Open season
Best October-May, with the clearest conditions in autumn and spring. Avoid the June-September monsoon because landslides and saturated trails are common.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Gangtok | Guide vehicle | ~2h30
Bagdogra airport | Car | ~4h

    Source: Government of Sikkim adventure tourism.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="26.996500" lon="88.267000">
    <name>Darjeeling / Senchal MTB (West Bengal, IN) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <desc>Tea-hill and forest descents beneath Kanchenjunga views

    Trails
Steep estate roads, rocky village tracks and forest routes around Darjeeling, Senchal and Tiger Hill create short technical descents and longer cross-country days. Many attractive paths are hiking trails, protected forest or private tea-estate land, so legal route selection matters.

    Getting up / price
No lift. Use a local cycling guide and vehicle drop where permitted. The Rangeet Valley cable car is a sightseeing installation and should not be assumed to carry mountain bikes.

    Open season
Best October-May. Monsoon rain from June-September brings deep mud, poor visibility and landslide risk.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Darjeeling | Bike / guide vehicle | ~30 min
Bagdogra airport | Car | ~3h

    Regional riding pin based around Senchal. See Incredible India - Darjeeling and verify every off-road section locally.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="12.030000" lon="108.440000">
    <name>Da Lat Pine Forest MTB (Vietnam) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <desc>Vietnam's cool-climate pine-forest riding hub

    Trails
Dirt roads and natural trails north of Da Lat cross the Langbiang Plateau through pine forest, farms and rolling highland terrain. Routes can be linked into technical singletrack and longer cross-country days, but there is no signed gravity bike park.

    Getting up / price
No lift. Rent locally or book a guide and vehicle transfer from Da Lat. Bidoup-Nui Ba and other protected areas require adherence to park access rules.

    Open season
Best December-April in the drier season. May-November rain makes red dirt and roots slippery, although guided rides operate year-round when conditions permit.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Da Lat centre | Bike / shuttle | ~25 min
Da Lat airport | Car | ~45 min

    Source: Vietnam Tourism, which recommends mountain biking the pine-forest dirt trails north of the city.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="22.336000" lon="103.844000">
    <name>Sapa Valley MTB (Vietnam) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <desc>Rice-terrace and mountain-village riding in northern Vietnam

    Trails
Steep roads, buffalo tracks and mixed dirt paths descend through rice terraces and Hmong villages around Sapa and the Muong Hoa valley. The riding is scenic and culturally sensitive rather than park-built, ranging from accessible valley tours to technical wet singletrack.

    Getting up / price
No lift. Mountain-bike rental and guided tours are available in Sapa; use a local guide for village access, route finding and point-to-point vehicle support.

    Open season
Best in April-May and September-October. Summer is hot and wet; winter can be cold, foggy and occasionally icy at altitude.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Sapa centre | Bike | Immediate
Hanoi | Bus / train + van | ~5-8h

    Source: Vietnam Tourism. Ride respectfully through working farms and villages.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="61.231000" lon="10.453000">
    <name>Hafjell Bike Park (Norway) [lift]</name>
    <desc>Norway's benchmark lift-served downhill park

    Trails
Seventeen green-to-black trails cover roughly 28 km, mixing long machine-built flow, jump lines and World Cup-grade technical downhill over substantial vertical. Roller Coaster alone packs 60 jumps and 36 berms.

    Getting up / price
Gondola and chairlift uplift with rentals at the base. Current day-pass prices vary by date; buy through the operator.

    Open season
Typically mid-June to mid-October: weekends at each end and daily in high summer.
Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:00
Typical published hours; operating days vary across the season.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Lillehammer | Car / bus | ~20 min
Oslo | Car | ~2h30

    Source: official Hafjell Bike Park.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="61.306500" lon="12.164500">
    <name>Trysil Bike Park (Norway) [chairlift]</name>
    <desc>Large progression-focused trail destination at Trysilfjellet

    Trails
Lift-served flow trails with berms, jumps and drops connect to the wider Trysil Bike Arena, including around 30 km of built trails near the main centre. Options range from family progression to fast expert lines.

    Getting up / price
Fjellekspressen chairlift carries bikes; a bike pass is required. Pedal-access trail networks remain available beyond lift days.

    Open season
Published 2026 lift season: selected dates from 5 June through 11 October, daily 20 June-16 August and during autumn holidays.
Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:00
Published standard lift hours; selected evening extensions apply.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Oslo | Car / bus | ~2h45

    Source: official 2026 summer lift schedule.</desc>
