  <wpt lat="-42.755381" lon="146.628367">
    <name>Maydena Bike Park (Tasmania, AU) [95 AUD uplift + mountain pass]</name>
    <desc>Australia's largest gravity bike park and Red Bull Hardline Tasmania venue

    Trails
More than 85 gravity trails descend up to 820 vertical metres from the summit and midline shuttle drops. The network mixes long natural enduro lines, race-speed downhill, large jump and drop trails, plus skills areas; summit uplift is intended for intermediate to advanced riders.

    Red Bull Hardline
Maydena has hosted the Southern Hemisphere edition of Red Bull Hardline since 2024, including the 7-8 February 2026 event. Its invitation-only Hardline course combines World Cup-level downhill with enormous jumps and drops. The course and eastern park sector close around the event and are not available for unsanctioned riding or spectating outside published event access.

    Getting up / price
Truck uplift serves the summit and midline. The published 2026/27 adult summit uplift is 95 AUD; every rider also needs a separate Maydena Mountain Pass.

    Open season
Open from 3 October; closed from 29 June (published 2026/27 seasonal pattern, with varying weekly operating days).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00
Typical operating-day estimate; check the official calendar because uplift days and event closures vary.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Hobart | Car | ~1h15
Hobart Airport | Car | ~1h30

    Sources: official uplift and trail information, operating calendar and Red Bull Hardline Tasmania FAQ. Book ahead and verify closures.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.400900" lon="-123.198600">
    <name>Cypress Mountain Hardline venue (British Columbia) [event course, no public riding]</name>
    <desc>2026 Red Bull Hardline Canada venue above Vancouver's North Shore

    Trails
Cypress Mountain is building an invitation-only Hardline course for the first Canadian edition on 17 October 2026. The announced course combines extremely steep and rugged downhill, technical rock gardens, massive gaps and drops exceeding 10 metres.

    Getting up / price
No public bike uplift or public access to the Hardline course is confirmed. This pin documents the event venue, not a trail visitors can ride. Use established legal North Shore networks for normal riding.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; Red Bull Hardline is an invitation-only professional competition. Do not enter, inspect or ride the construction and race course unless the organizer explicitly permits access.

    Open season
The inaugural Canadian event is announced for 17 October 2026. This is not a recurring public riding season.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Vancouver | Car | ~35 min

    Sources: official Cypress Mountain announcement and Red Bull Hardline series. Event access and course status can change.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-33.046200" lon="-71.627600">
    <name>Valparaiso Cerro Abajo (Chile) [urban DH event course]</name>
    <desc>The original Red Bull Cerro Abajo urban downhill

    Event
Valparaiso turns its steep hills, narrow alleys, staircases, rooftops and historic funicular corridors into the world's best-known urban downhill course. The 22nd edition ran on 15 February 2026, descending from Cerro Carcel toward Plaza Anibal Pinto through nearly 280 steps, wallrides, drops and temporary jumps.

    Getting up / price
No uplift and no permanent marked race trail. Spectating is free during the event; outside race weekend these are public city streets and stairs, not a sanctioned MTB course.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; The race line and artificial features exist only under event control. Do not attempt the course outside an authorized event.

    Open season
The documented 2026 event ran on 15 February. There is no public riding season.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Santiago | Bus / car | ~1h45

    Sources: official 2026 event page and official series format.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.426500" lon="8.938100">
    <name>Genova Cerro Abajo (Italy) [urban DH event course]</name>
    <desc>Red Bull Cerro Abajo from Monte Peralto to the old city

    Event
The 2026 urban downhill dropped 279 m over 2.2 km from the Righi funicular top station at Monte Peralto to Largo della Zecca. Racers threaded ancient creuze and caruggi, staircases, tight bends, wallrides, drops and temporary obstacles. The 2026 edition ran on 27-28 June.

    Getting up / price
The Righi funicular reaches the start area, but it is not a bike uplift for a permanent race trail. Spectating is free during the event.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; This is an event-only course through public streets. Artificial features and a closed race line are not available for normal riding.

    Open season
The documented 2026 event ran on 27-28 June. There is no public riding season.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Genova Piazza Principe | Walk + funicular | ~25 min

    Sources: official 2026 event page and official course overview.</desc>
  </wpt>
