Loose, rocky and exposed desert singletrack in the hills above Pachacamac. Local classics include Prado, Terrucos, Jergon and other short, steep descents; Prado alone drops roughly 343 m with a black-diamond rating. Heat, dust, navigation and informal trail junctions make a local rider or guide valuable.

    Getting up / price
No lift and no unified trail fee. Pedal the desert roads and climbing lines or arrange a commercial guide and shuttle from Lima.

