Downtown Anchorage | Car | ~20 min

    Sources: official bike-park terrain and lift information and official tickets, pass and hours page. Check the current calendar and conditions.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="61.712161" lon="-149.296960">
    <name>Government Peak Recreation Area (Alaska) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Purpose-built Mat-Su singletrack beneath the Talkeetna Mountains

    Trails
Two dedicated singletrack trails leave the stadium area and total about 4.2 miles, climbing through forest before rolling downhill. The wider recreation area adds scenic multi-use terrain and views toward the Chugach Range. This is a compact pedal-access trail network, not the proposed downhill ski development on the other side of Government Peak.

    Getting up / price
No lift or shuttle. Pedal the two-way singletrack from the chalet and yield to uphill riders and pedestrians. Borough parking is 5 USD per day or 40 USD for an annual pass according to the published trail brochure.

    Open season
Open from 1 June; closed from 1 October (typical dry-trail indication).
Daily opening hours: daylight only
Opening is condition-dependent. Do not ride saturated trails, and expect lingering snow or freeze-thaw outside midsummer.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Palmer | Car | ~25 min
Anchorage | Car | ~1h15

    Source: Matanuska-Susitna Borough trail description and status. Check the live Borough status before riding.</desc>
