  <wpt lat="61.155343" lon="-150.040198">
    <name>Kincaid Park Singletrack (Alaska) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Anchorage's large urban singletrack playground

    Trails
A dense network of roughly 39 miles of rolling trails, including purpose-built mountain-bike singletrack with banked turns, short punchy climbs and fast descents. It suits progression and energetic trail laps more than sustained downhill, but gives Anchorage a substantial all-level dirt network minutes from the city.

    Getting up / price
No lift, shuttle or trail ticket. Pedal interconnected loops from designated Kincaid trailheads and follow one-way signs where posted; the wider park is shared with walkers, runners and wildlife.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; Moose and bears occur inside the park. Carry appropriate deterrent, give wildlife a very wide berth and never ride closed or muddy trails.

    Open season
Open from 1 June; closed from 15 October (typical dirt-season indication).
Daily opening hours: daylight only
Actual dirt opening depends on snowmelt and drying. Winter fat-bike access follows separate grooming and trail rules.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Downtown Anchorage | Car / bike | ~20 min

    Source: Visit Anchorage's official Kincaid trail overview. Check local trail conditions and closures before riding.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="58.267771" lon="-134.509417">
    <name>Eaglecrest Flow Trail (Alaska) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Unsupervised downhill flow trail on Douglas Island

    Trails
Eaglecrest maintains a dedicated, signed downhill-only mountain-bike flow trail in its lush coastal mountain setting. The present summer offer is a pedal-access trail rather than the larger lift-served bike park shown in long-term development plans. Inspect features on the first lap and expect wet roots, soft ground and active mountain maintenance nearby.

    Getting up / price
No summer lift or supervised bike operation is documented. Pedal the service-road access from the ski-area base; riding is at your own risk and hikers are prohibited on the bike trail.

    Open season
Open from 15 June; closed from 1 October (typical snow-free indication).
Daily opening hours: daylight only
There is no formal bike-park calendar. Obey posted closures and check the current mountain report because snow, saturated ground and maintenance can block access.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Downtown Juneau | Car | ~20 min

    Sources: official Eaglecrest mountain-bike flow-trail rules and official mountain conditions. The winter chairs should not be assumed to carry bikes.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-0.993186" lon="36.652367">
    <name>Kereita Forest MTB Park (Kenya) [no lift, shuttle days]</name>
    <desc>Kenya's established downhill and enduro forest venue

    Trails
Maintained mountain-bike trails wind through high-elevation Kereita Forest on the Aberdare slopes. The network includes purpose-built descents, technical forest riding and a skills area, with loops ranging from approachable trail riding to intermediate and expert gravity terrain.

    Getting up / price
No mechanical lift. Pedal the loops or confirm locally advertised Saturday shuttle laps. Published 2026 indications are around 300 KES forest entry and 500 KES for the trails; bike hire and coaching are available through the operator.

    Open season
Open from 1 January with no formal seasonal closure.
Daily opening hours: 08:00-17:00
Estimated venue hours. Heavy rain makes roots and soil extremely slippery; confirm opening, shuttle operation and fees before travelling.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Nairobi | Car | ~1h15

    Sources: The Forest's official mountain-biking page and Cycle Africa's 2026 Kereita trail and shuttle guide. Confirm forest conditions and access locally.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="0.239637" lon="37.299980">
    <name>Borana / Mount Kenya Enduro (Kenya) [no lift, access by event or guide]</name>
    <desc>Highland enduro stages beneath Mount Kenya

    Trails
The private Borana landscape near Nanyuki has hosted the Mount Kenya 10to4 challenge and documented enduro stages. Expect dry rocky singletrack, fast savanna tracks and rolling descents at altitude. Wildlife and private conservancy management make this an organized-event or guided destination, not a public trailhead.

    Getting up / price
No lift. Race support, pedalling and event vehicles provide access depending on the itinerary. Obtain explicit permission from the conservancy or a current event organizer before bringing a bike.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; Never ride independently among wildlife or enter conservancy land without authorization. Follow ranger instructions and use an established local organizer.

    Open season
Open from 1 June; closed from 1 November (drier-season indication).
Daily opening hours: guided access only
There is no public operating calendar. Access, wildlife management and rain conditions control whether riding is possible.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
