  <wpt lat="-4.123097" lon="15.565706">
    <name>Mount Mangengenge (DR Congo) [scouting only, access unverified]</name>
    <desc>Steep Crystal Mountains objective outside Kinshasa

    Trails
Mount Mangengenge rises to about 718 m southeast of Kinshasa and is reached by rough tracks from the Sainte Angèle de Mérici side. The mountain has the gradient and broken access tracks for exploratory enduro, but no maintained MTB trail, current riding operator or dependable public route is documented.

    Getting up / price
No lift, shuttle or trail fee is documented. Do not treat this pin as a ready-to-ride trailhead: arrange local permission, an experienced contact, secure transport and a verified route before considering a visit.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; Access and personal security can change quickly in DRC. Official advice recommends experienced local organizations outside major towns and warns against unsupervised off-road travel. Do not ride here independently.

    Open season
Open from 1 June; closed from 1 October (drier-season indication only).
Daily opening hours: guided daylight access only
No MTB operating season exists. Additions to this entry should include a verified local club, route and land permission.

