    <desc>Lift-accessed Caucasus downhill above the Georgian Military Highway

    Trails
Gudauri's high alpine summer terrain includes marked bike routes and a documented downhill trail of roughly 4.8 km. Open grassland, loose rock and big mountain weather create a raw resort experience rather than a dense machine-built park.

    Getting up / price
Designated summer lifts carry bicycles. Published indications are 15 GEL for a Gudauri lift ride, with the Gudauri, Kobi, Firni and Truso installations operating in the main summer period; verify which lift and trail are active on the day.

    Open season
Open from 1 July; closed from 16 September (published typical summer-lift window).
Daily opening hours: 11:00-17:00
Wind, storms and maintenance can close exposed lifts without notice. Confirm bike carriage and current trail marking.

