    <desc>Marked coastal-mountain trails southeast of Muscat

    Trails
A locally built network around GECO Camp and Jebel Sifah Resort combines graded beginner and intermediate loops, coastal tracks and wadi-side riding. Guided programs can extend into more technical singletrack and enduro-style terrain, making this Oman's clearest organized trail-center offer.

    Getting up / price
No lift. Pedal the loops or book a guided itinerary. Published unguided access with mountain bike, helmet, map and basic mechanical support costs 15 OMR per person per hour; guided rates vary.

    Open season
Open from 15 October; closed from 1 May (cooler-season indication).
Daily opening hours: 07:00-18:00
Estimated daylight operation. Extreme heat makes summer riding unsafe; flash floods can affect wadis even when local skies look clear.

