Local riders use the forested northern valleys and open southern slopes of the Bogd Khan reserve for natural downhill and trail riding. Routes toward Tsetsee Gun involve steep climbing, rock gardens and shared hiking paths; there is no official bike park, trail grading or unified MTB map.

    Getting up / price
No lift or established shuttle. Pedal from the city edge or arrange a local rider or guide who knows current reserve rules and suitable descents.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; This is a protected nature reserve. Use only routes currently open to bicycles, avoid fragile or muddy ground and yield to every walker. Seasonal closures occur.

