Community-recorded MTB loops use the roads and paths around Banco National Park's lake and Maison de la Nature, creating about 20 km of rolling forest riding with roughly 210 m of climbing. It is cross-country leaning rather than a gravity park, but includes short natural descents in dense tropical forest.

