A former LAMCO mountain road climbs through East Nimba Nature Reserve past Blue Lake, changing from rainforest to savanna and exposed former mining terrain. Liberia's tourism authority explicitly identifies the trail for bikers, hikers and drivers; side trails and the tri-border route require reserve guidance.

    Getting up / price
No lift. Register and pay the entrance fee at the Nimba Ecolodge and Reserve reception, then arrange a guide and confirm whether vehicle support is allowed for the intended route.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; This is a protected biodiversity reserve. Remain on the authorized road or guide-approved trail, avoid wet ground and follow every ranger instruction.

