The Western Area Peninsula Forest Reserve rises sharply behind Freetown, with rough mountain roads and hiking routes toward Picket Hill, Mount Gabon and coastal villages. The terrain is potentially compelling for natural enduro, but no signed MTB network, maintained descent or dependable bicycle guide is documented.

