The Djibloho community route is a 9.2 km mountain-bike loop with about 104 m of climbing around the planned city formerly known as Oyala. It offers rolling tropical dirt-road and track exploration, not a signed bike park or sustained downhill venue. Only a handful of public MTB recordings exist in the country, so current local knowledge is essential.

