    <desc>Rwanda's signature Lake Kivu mountain-bike journey

    Trails
The Congo Nile Trail follows roughly 227 km of steep lakeside country from Rubavu toward Rusizi through tea and coffee landscapes, villages and beaches. Its four to seven stages mix unpaved roads, rough tracks, sustained climbs and natural descents; it is an expedition-style MTB route, not a shaped bike park.

    Getting up / price
No lift. Ride point-to-point with luggage transfer or book a local guide, rental bike and support vehicle. The marker identifies the usual northern start in Rubavu.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; Carry offline navigation and repair equipment. Confirm the current itinerary and advice near the DRC border, and never cross an international border accidentally.

    Open season
Open from 1 June; closed from 1 October (principal dry-season indication).
Daily opening hours: daylight riding only
The route is available year-round, but rain substantially changes dirt-road and trail conditions.

