    Sources: the official Gishwati-Mukura tourism plan listing the Mukura Bike Trail and the Rwanda Development Board cycling program. Confirm access with park authorities.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-20.487139" lon="57.479437">
    <name>Mo'Bike Chamouny (Mauritius) [4x4 shuttle]</name>
    <desc>Mauritius's first dedicated mountain-bike park

    Trails
More than 25 km across at least 12 professionally built and maintained trails descend about 350 m through forest toward the south coast. Green, blue and red lines range from easy flow to roots, jumps, steep technical sections and enduro race stages.

    Getting up / price
A 4x4 carries riders and bikes uphill every 30-45 minutes. A three-hour pass provides unlimited runs; rentals and protective equipment are available, while riders with a suitable MTB can buy trail access only. Book the current package and price online.

    Open season
Open from 1 January with no seasonal closure (normally open year-round).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00 Wednesday-Sunday
Closed Monday and Tuesday. Heavy rain or cyclonic conditions can close the park.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Sir Seewoosagur Ramgoolam Airport | Car | ~50 min
Bel Ombre | Car | ~15 min

    Source: official Mo'Bike trail, shuttle, booking and opening-hours information. Reserve a session and check weather closure status before travelling.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-20.364848" lon="57.704840">
    <name>Vallée de Ferney MTB (Mauritius) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Authorized conservation-valley bike routes

    Trails
La Vallée de Ferney permits bicycles on its open tracks through native forest and grassland. Four routes cover 5, 8, 13 and 18 km; the longest gains about 970 m and is rated difficult. This is scenic trail and cross-country riding with natural descents, not a bike park, and riders must bring their own bikes.

    Getting up / price
No lift or shuttle. Pedal each loop from the reserve reception. Published admission is 500 MUR per visiting adult and 250 MUR per child, with lower resident rates.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; Stay on authorized open tracks in this conservation area. Access can be restricted for private events between June and September, and weather can close routes.

    Open season
Open from 1 January with no seasonal closure (normally open year-round).
Daily opening hours: activities 08:30-14:00; reception until 17:00
Latest permitted start varies by route, from 10:30 for 18 km to 14:00 for 5 km. Book ahead.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Mahébourg | Car | ~20 min

    Source: official Ferney bicycle access, routes, prices and opening hours. Confirm route availability when booking.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-21.070667" lon="55.387953">
    <name>Maïdo Megavalanche Descent (Réunion) [shuttle]</name>
    <desc>Iconic mass-start descent from the Maïdo highlands

    Trails
The Maïdo descent is Réunion's internationally known Mégavalanche venue and a major mass start race course. Its huge drop toward the west coast crosses exposed volcanic highland, tamarind forest and increasingly tropical lower slopes, with fast, rough and technical terrain for experienced riders.

    Getting up / price
No permanent lift, but commercial shuttle and guided services run from the west coast. Arrange an uplift and current route guidance rather than attempting an unsupported road return.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; This is a long mountain descent, not a continuously maintained park line. Fog, rain, erosion, forestry closures and mixed-use sections can change it quickly; verify every segment and carry repair equipment.

    Open season
Open from 1 May; closed from 1 December (cooler and generally drier-season indication).
Daily opening hours: guided daylight access only
No fixed operating calendar; shuttle schedules and forest closures determine access.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Saint-Gilles-les-Bains | Booked MTB shuttle | ~1h15

    Sources: the official Réunion tourism MTB guide naming the Maïdo Mégavalanche and shuttle and a local Maïdo guided operator. Check ONF closures before riding.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-21.190605" lon="55.635633">
    <name>Station VTT du Volcan (Réunion) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>126 km of graded volcanic mountain-bike routes

    Trails
The official Volcan MTB station has 12 rehabilitated circuits across 126 km on the Piton de la Fournaise massif; all 12 official ONF traces are drawn on this map. Green, blue, red and black routes support loop, descent and enduro riding through pasture, forest and stark volcanic landscapes. The marker is at Piton Textor, the principal hub and official start for six circuits.

    Getting up / price
No bike lift or permanent uplift is documented. Pedal the signed loops or arrange a local guide and vehicle for a route designed as a descent. Public trail access is generally free.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; Volcanic activity, fire risk, fog and ONF forestry orders can close roads or trails without warning. Use the official carto-guide and obey every closure.

    Open season
Open from 1 May; closed from 1 December (cooler and generally drier-season indication).
Daily opening hours: daylight only
The network is normally year-round when authorized, but exposed high routes are weather dependent.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Saint-Pierre | Car to Piton Textor | ~1h15

    Source: the official ONF Volcan circuit guide, trailheads and GPX downloads. Check volcanic and forestry access before departure.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-21.131876" lon="55.496038">
    <name>Station VTT de Cilaos (Réunion) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Nine graded circuits inside Réunion's mountain cirque

    Trails
Cilaos has an official MTB station with nine mapped circuits for multiple ability levels; all nine official ONF traces are drawn on this map. Routes combine highland roads, forest tracks and natural technical descents beneath the cirque's immense volcanic walls; this is a signed trail network rather than a shaped downhill park. The marker is at the Mare à Joseph trail hub, where the largest group of individual circuits starts.

    Getting up / price
No bike lift or permanent shuttle is documented. Pedal from Cilaos or book a local guide and vehicle where permitted. Trail access is generally free.

&amp;#9888;&amp;#65039; The cirque is steep, exposed and prone to rockfall, landslides and abrupt weather. Check the official map, road access and ONF trail closures before riding.

    Open season
Open from 1 May; closed from 1 December (cooler and generally drier-season indication).
Daily opening hours: daylight only
The network is normally year-round when routes are authorized and conditions permit.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Saint-Louis | Car via Route de Cilaos | ~1h15

    Source: the official ONF Cilaos circuit guide and nine GPX downloads. Verify current closures locally.</desc>
  </wpt>
