  <wpt lat="-44.876000" lon="168.940000">
    <name>Cardrona Bike Park (New Zealand) [184 NZD]</name>
    <desc>Cardrona 1860 m - NZ's highest bike park, McDougall's Chondola top

    Trails
Ten kilometres of peak-to-pub downhill with 345 m of vertical drop, plus a network of flow and technical lines at the South Island's highest lift-served park. The Whitestar Express chairlift opens additional expert terrain above the gondola mid-station. The famous Cardrona pub is the finish line.

    Getting up / price
The McDougall's Chondola and Whitestar Express chairlift carry bikes during the summer season. 2026 day pass NZ$184 adult, with multi-day and season options available. Bike rental and guiding at the base.

    Open season
Open from December; closed from March (southern hemisphere summer).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:00
Estimated hours; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Queenstown | Car | ~1h
Wanaka | Car | ~35 min

    Source: Cardrona.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-37.146000" lon="146.449000">
    <name>Mt Buller Bike Park (Victoria, AU) [chairlift]</name>
    <desc>Mt Buller - Victoria's lift-served alpine gravity park

    Trails
A network of downhill and enduro trails descending from the alpine village at 1600 m through snow gum forest. Purpose-built flow lines and technical black descents make use of the ski-area chairlift infrastructure during the green summer months.

    Getting up / price
Chairlift access for bikes during summer operation. Confirm the current bike ticket, lift schedule and trail status with Mt Buller before travelling.

    Open season
Open from December; closed from March (southern hemisphere summer).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Estimated hours; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Melbourne | Car | ~3h

    Source: Mt Buller.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="60.629000" lon="6.421000">
    <name>Voss Bike Park (Norway) [gondola]</name>
    <desc>Voss Gondola top 820 m - home of Ekstremsportveko

    Trails
Norway's extreme sports capital, hosting the annual Ekstremsportveko festival. The gondola-served park has downhill and enduro trails with views over Voss lake and the surrounding fjords. Purpose-built lines range from blue flow to World-Cup-proven technical black descents.

    Getting up / price
The Voss Gondola carries bikes from the town centre (50 m) to the top station at 820 m. Confirm the current bike ticket and season with Voss Resort.

    Open season
Open from June; closed from October (estimated summer season).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Estimated hours; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Bergen | Train / car | ~1h30
Voss centre | Gondola | ~5 min

    Source: Voss Resort.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="60.536000" lon="8.009000">
    <name>Geilo Bike Park (Norway) [chairlift]</name>
    <desc>Geilo - lift-served riding between Oslo and Bergen

    Trails
A growing bike park in the Hallingdal valley with chairlift-served downhill and flow trails through mountain birch forest. Trail progression from green to black, with the ski resort's natural terrain providing long descents.

    Getting up / price
Chairlift carries bikes during summer operation. Check the current bike ticket with Geilo Sommer before travelling.

    Open season
Open from June; closed from October (estimated summer season).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Estimated hours; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Oslo | Train | ~3h30
Bergen | Train | ~2h30

    Source: Geilo.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="60.848340" lon="8.511480">
    <name>Hemsedal Rides (Norway) [chairlift]</name>
    <desc>Lift-served flow and technical riding above Hemsedal

    Trails
Hollvin Express serves the Hemsedal Rides network, including the long blue Silverstone descent, green Broadway connector and the more technical red High Line. Tottelia Bike Park at the resort base adds compact progression trails and skills features.

    Getting up / price
Hollvin Express carries bikes to roughly 1,150 m. A SkiStar BikePass is required; rental and instruction are available at the resort.

    Open season
Published 2026 lift season: daily 27 June-16 August, plus selected September weekends and daily 26 September-4 October.
Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:00
Some autumn dates operate 11:00-15:00 or 11:00-16:00; check the live schedule and trail status.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Hemsedal centre | Bike / bus / car | ~10 min
Oslo | Car / bus | ~3h

    Sources: SkiStar Hemsedal biking, official 2026 opening dates and Hemsedal's verified Silverstone listing. Pin marks the published Silverstone start near the lift top at 1,151 m.</desc>
  </wpt>
