  <wpt lat="60.532437" lon="9.059966">
    <name>Nesbyen MTB (Norway) [shuttle]</name>
    <desc>Norway's best-known shuttle-served gravity trail hub

    Trails
Nesbyen combines rough natural enduro descents around Trytetjern with purpose-built trails for several levels. HallingSpranget is the signature blue route: 17 km from Syningen on Nesfjellet to the town centre, losing about 1,000 vertical metres.

    Getting up / price
Trailhead Nesbyen runs fixed-route gravity shuttles between Blingsmovegen and Trytetjern. The separate FjellLinken bike bus serves the HallingSpranget start; advance booking is recommended.

    Open season
Typically May-October, depending on snow and trail conditions. HallingSpranget is aiming for an early June opening in 2026, with bookings available from 13 June and daily summer shuttle service.
Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:30
Typical gravity-shuttle window; HallingSpranget bus times and autumn operating days differ.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Nesbyen centre | Bike shuttle | ~25-40 min to trailheads
Oslo | Train / car | ~2h30-3h

    Sources: Trailhead Nesbyen shuttle and official HallingSpranget site. Pin marks the OSM-mapped HallingSpranget start at Syningen, officially described as roughly 1,100 m.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="66.165000" lon="29.170000">
    <name>Ruka Bike Park (Finland) [gondola]</name>
    <desc>Ruka - Lapland's largest lift-served bike park

    Trails
Finland's premier gravity destination with gondola-served downhill and enduro trails through Lapland's fell landscape. The long summer days above the Arctic Circle mean riding until late evening in June and July, and the rock-and-root terrain is distinctively Finnish.

    Getting up / price
The Ruka gondola carries bikes during the summer season. Confirm the current bike pass and lift schedule with Ruka before travelling.

    Open season
Open from June; closed from October (estimated summer season).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-19:00
Estimated hours; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Kuusamo airport | Car / bus | ~30 min
Oulu | Car | ~2h30

    Source: Ruka.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.796000" lon="6.928000">
    <name>Courmayeur Bike Park (Aosta Valley, IT) [cable car]</name>
    <desc>Courmayeur - lift-served gravity at the foot of Mont Blanc

    Trails
A cable-car-served bike park in the shadow of Mont Blanc with downhill and enduro lines through forest and alpine terrain. The Plan Checrouit area above Courmayeur offers one of the most spectacular backdrops in European mountain biking.

    Getting up / price
The Courmayeur cable car carries bikes during summer operation. Check the current bike ticket and lift schedule with Courmayeur Mont Blanc before travelling.

    Open season
Open from June; closed from September (estimated summer season).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Estimated hours; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Aosta | Car / bus | ~45 min
Geneva | Car | ~1h30

    Source: Courmayeur.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.956000" lon="6.881000">
    <name>Sestriere Bike Park (Via Lattea, IT) [chairlift]</name>
    <desc>Sestriere 2035 m - Via Lattea lift-served park

    Trails
Part of the Via Lattea (Milky Way) ski area shared with Sauze d'Oulx, Sestriere offers chairlift-served downhill and enduro trails at over 2000 m altitude. The high-alpine terrain and long descents toward the valley make it one of Piedmont's primary gravity destinations.

    Getting up / price
Chairlift access for bikes during summer operation. The Via Lattea bike pass may also cover neighbouring resorts. Confirm the current tariff with Sestriere before travelling.

    Open season
Open from July; closed from August (short high-alpine summer window).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
