  <wpt lat="49.172600" lon="13.209060">
    <name>Bikepark Spicak (Sumava, CZ) [940 CZK]</name>
    <desc>Spicak 1198 m - top of the Spicak chairlift

    Trails
The biggest bike park in Czechia and the one Czech and German riders treat as home. Around a dozen lines off a 330 m vertical: green flow, the long Traverz, several red jump lines and black rock and root tech, plus a dirt-jump area and a 4X track at the base. A second chairlift climbs on to Pancir 1214 m for the longer natural descents. Dense Sumava spruce forest, so it rides well in the heat and turns greasy fast in the wet.

    Getting up / price
The Spicak chairlift from Zelezna Ruda carries bikes; a day ticket is 940 CZK for adults, 800 CZK for youth and 420 CZK for children, and tickets are issued on a chip card with a 50 CZK refundable deposit. Five-ride tickets (700 CZK) suit a short visit. The park is in the Gravity Card network.

    Open season
Open from 1 May; closed from 1 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions). Weekends only in May, then daily from 15 June.
Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

