  <wpt lat="47.135590" lon="9.743130">
    <name>Bikepark Brandnertal (Vorarlberg, AT) [58 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Loischkopf 1780 m - top of the Loischkopfbahn

    Trails
About 30 km of trail spread across the Loischkopf and Tschengla side of the Brandnertal, and one of the best-built parks in western Austria. Family flow lines, long red jump trails and proper technical downhill, with the two lower-mountain trails - Tschengla Unchained (blue) and Tschaeck the Ripper (red) - rebuilt from scratch for 2026, plus a new kids' area with its own conveyor in the finish zone. Trails ST04 and ST05 stay shut until 15 June each year to protect a grouse population.

    Getting up / price
A new 10-seat gondola with bike cabins runs Tschengla to Loischkopf; the Dorfbahn in Brand and the Panoramabahn add terrain. Adult day ticket 58 EUR (junior 47, child 31), four-hour 50 EUR, season 468 EUR or 680 EUR with the Gravity Card. Children born 2020 or later ride free.

    Open season
Open from 14 May; closed from 1 November (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:45
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Zurich | Car | ~1h45
Bregenz | Car | ~45 min

    Source: Bikepark Brandnertal.
