    <desc>Penken 1790 m - top of the Penkenbahn

    Trails
The Zillertal's gravity centre, and home of the Hoellenritt - a purpose-built singletrail that drops the full mountain back to Mayrhofen and is one of the longest of its kind in the Alps. Himmelfahrt is the second signature line. Above them the Penken plateau feeds panorama routes and all-mountain trails, and the Ahorn on the far side of the valley adds more. Not a lines-and-berms bike park so much as a very large lift-served trail mountain.

    Getting up / price
The Penkenbahn from Mayrhofen carries bikes, backed up by the Horbergbahn and the Finkenberger Almbahn. The Action Day Ticket for bikers is 72.50 EUR (63 EUR with the Zillertal guest card, 31.50 EUR child); a plain up-and-down is 40 EUR and a single ride 28 EUR.

    Open season
Open from 23 May; closed from 4 October (published 2026 dates).
Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Innsbruck | Car | ~1h00
Munich | Car | ~2h15

    Source: Mayrhofner Bergbahnen.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.163420" lon="11.860640">
    <name>Mayrhofen: Penkenbahn valley station</name>
    <desc>Penkenbahn valley station in Mayrhofen, 650 m - where the Hoellenritt finishes.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.175960" lon="11.816040">
    <name>Mayrhofen: Penken summit</name>
    <desc>Top of the Kombibahn Penken at 1985 m, the high point of the Penken lift network.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.257930" lon="12.715180">
    <name>Kaprun - Maiskogel and Kitzsteinhorn (Salzburg, AT) [35 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Maiskogel 1570 m - top of the MK Maiskogelbahn

    Trails
Two very different halves. The Maiskogel Trail is 4.6 km of wide berms, rollers and small jumps straight back to Kaprun - the friendliest introduction to gravity riding in the Pinzgau. Above it the Kitzsteinhorn freeride trails start from the glacier terminal at nearly 3000 m and drop through high alpine scree and rock to the Alpincenter, which is about as high as lift-served riding gets in Austria and stays rideable when the valleys are baking.

    Getting up / price
Bike carriage is included in the ticket on the Maiskogelbahn, the 3K K-onnection and the Gletscherjet. Adult day ticket 35 EUR (child 17.50 EUR); a single ride up is 16.50 EUR.

    Open season
Open from 23 May; closed from 4 October (published 2026 dates). The glacier trails open later and depend on snow.
Daily opening hours: 08:30-16:30
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Salzburg | Car | ~1h20
Munich | Car | ~2h20

    Source: Kitzsteinhorn.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.273740" lon="12.756670">
    <name>Kaprun: Maiskogelbahn valley station</name>
    <desc>MK Maiskogelbahn valley station in Kaprun, 765 m - the end of the Maiskogel Trail.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.221010" lon="12.699320">
    <name>Kitzsteinhorn: Langwied / Alpincenter</name>
    <desc>Langwied at 1970 m, the hub between the Gletscherjet and the 3K K-onnection and the finish of the freeride trails.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.296790" lon="6.509540">
    <name>Bikepark Belleville - Les Menuires and Val Thorens (Savoie, FR) [26.70 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Pointe de la Masse 2770 m - top of the La Masse gondola

    Trails
The Belleville valley - Les Menuires, Saint-Martin and Val Thorens - runs over 100 km of marked trail between 1400 and 2800 m, the highest lift-served riding in the Trois Vallees. Easy Rider and Kiss Cool are the approachable descents; High Line and B'Hell'Ville Line are the serious ones, and a large enduro network links the three villages. From La Masse the descent is unbroken from 2770 m to 1400 m, all of it above or at the treeline.

    Getting up / price
The Pointe de la Masse gondola from Les Menuires is the key lift; Bruyeres and the Val Thorens lifts extend the terrain. A VTT day pass for the Trois Vallees bike area is 26.70 EUR, and winter season-pass holders get summer lift access included.

    Open season
Open from 5 July; closed from 31 August (published 2026 dates - a short high-summer season).
Daily opening hours: 09:15-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Geneva | Car | ~2h30
Moutiers | Train + bus | ~1h00

    Source: Les Menuires.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.318410" lon="6.535370">
    <name>Les Menuires: La Croisette</name>
    <desc>La Croisette at 1735 m - valley station of the Pointe de la Masse gondola and the resort's bike hub.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.318320" lon="6.578560">
    <name>Belleville: Bruyeres 2 top</name>
    <desc>Top of the Bruyeres 2 gondola at 2830 m, the other high entry point into the Belleville trail network.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="53.012900" lon="-3.936040">
    <name>Antur Stiniog (Eryri / Snowdonia, Wales) [44 GBP]</name>
    <desc>Uplift drop-off 470 m - above Blaenau Ffestiniog

    Trails
Fourteen downhill tracks cut into old slate workings above Blaenau Ffestiniog, green through to black, and there is no pedalling to them - the uplift is the only way up. Around 200 m of vertical per run, which sounds modest until you find the tracks are steep, rocky and relentless. Big tabletops and doubles on the graded jump lines, raw slate and roots on the black tracks. Five minutes up, ten to twenty down, and up to twenty runs in a day.

    Getting up / price
Van uplift only, roughly 40 to 44 GBP for the day; the trails cannot be ridden without it. Full facilities at the visitor centre: cafe, bike wash, showers and parking. Book ahead, it sells out.

    Open season
Open all year (uplift days are typically Thursday to Sunday; check the calendar before travelling).
Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Manchester | Car | ~2h15
Llandudno | Car | ~1h00

    Source: Antur Stiniog.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="53.006590" lon="-3.940540">
    <name>Antur Stiniog: visitor centre</name>
    <desc>Visitor centre and uplift pick-up at 270 m in Blaenau Ffestiniog - cafe, bike wash, showers, parking.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.815600" lon="-3.409510">
    <name>Revolution Bike Park (Llangynog, Wales) [50 GBP]</name>
    <desc>Llangynog 280 m - Revolution Bike Park, van uplift to the top

    Trails
Over 20 km of trail on a steep Berwyn hillside, and the reason people drive here is the jump lines: some of the biggest built anywhere in the UK. Alongside them sit raw, rooty natural tracks that stay genuinely hard in the wet, which in mid Wales is most of the time. This is not a beginner venue - full-face helmets and knee pads are compulsory for everyone.

    Getting up / price
Van uplift, 50 GBP for the day, or 15 GBP for a push-up pass; extra single lifts are 5 GBP each subject to space, with day-ticket holders given priority. Booking in advance on the website is required.

    Open season
Open all year, Friday to Sunday (check the website - conditions close the hill).
Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Manchester | Car | ~2h00
Shrewsbury | Car | ~1h10

    Source: Revolution Bike Park.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="53.012280" lon="-8.001320">
    <name>Bike Park Ireland (Co. Tipperary, IE) [uplift rate unverified]</name>
    <desc>Ballingarry 120 m - Bike Park Ireland, truck uplift to the top

    Trails
Ireland's only full gravity bike park with a proper uplift service. Six downhill trails from green to black plus a pro line, eight uplifted tracks in all, a large pump track and an cross-country loop, cut into wooded hillside in north Tipperary. The vertical is small but the tracks are well built and there is enough black-grade tech to keep experienced riders honest.

    Getting up / price
Three ex-army trucks, each with 30 seats and a bike trailer, run to the top every 15 minutes; a ticket covers park entry plus unlimited uplifts, in half-day or full-day form. We could not reach the operator's current price list, so no rate is recorded here - check bike-parkireland.ie.

    Open season
Open all year, every weekend (office Tuesday to Sunday; weekday riding by arrangement).
Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Dublin | Car | ~1h45
Limerick | Car | ~1h00

    Source: Bike Park Ireland.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.738010" lon="-118.930160">
    <name>Big White Bike Park (British Columbia, CA) [59 CAD]</name>
    <desc>Bullet Express top 2145 m - the bike park's unload

    Trails
The Okanagan's lift-served park, sitting high enough at 2145 m that it rides cool and dry through a British Columbia summer. Machine-built flow and jump lines dominate, with steeper technical tracks through the sub-alpine spruce below them, and around 480 m of vertical to the village. Quiet compared with the coastal parks, and the trail surface - fine volcanic soil - is genuinely good.

    Getting up / price
The day ticket includes unlimited lift access on the Bullet Express and is 59 CAD for adults aged 19-64, plus GST. Season passes are sold through the resort's online store. Friday evening extended riding is included on the day when it runs.

    Open season
Open from 1 July; closed from 8 September (published 2026 dates - a short, reliable high-summer season).
Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Kelowna | Car | ~1h00

    Source: Big White Ski Resort.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
