  <wpt lat="-40.208370" lon="-71.303960">
    <name>Chapelco Bike Park (Neuquen, AR) [summer rate unverified]</name>
    <desc>Cota 1600 - top of the Telecabina Chapelco

    Trails
Seven marked descents for every level, dropping through lenga forest on the flank of Cerro Chapelco above San Martin de los Andes. A new ten-seat gondola opened for 2026, linking the base to Cota 1600 in about five minutes and carrying up to 3000 people an hour, which transforms how many laps a day is worth. Southern-hemisphere season, so it runs while the Alps are shut.

    Getting up / price
Unlimited gondola laps with a bike pass; bring your own bike and helmet. The operator publishes winter skiing rates well ahead but had not posted a summer bike-park tariff at the time of writing, so no price is recorded here - check cerrochapelco.com.ar.

    Open season
Open from 15 December; closed from 16 April (typical southern-summer window; confirm dates with the operator).
Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
San Martin de los Andes | Car | ~30 min
Bariloche | Car | ~2h30

    Source: Cerro Chapelco.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
