  <wpt lat="-44.673200" lon="169.003760">
    <name>Bike Glendhu (Wanaka, NZ) [38 NZD]</name>
    <desc>Glendhu Bay 310 m - Bike Glendhu base, shuttles to the summit

    Trails
Close to 40 km of purpose-built trail on a working high-country sheep station above Lake Wanaka, opened in 2020 and already one of the best trail networks in New Zealand. Long, cruisey scenic climbs and descents for beginners at the bottom, hard singletrack and jump lines higher up, and the whole thing looks out over the lake and the Southern Alps. Dry schist soil that rides year-round.

    Getting up / price
A day trail pass is 38 NZD for adults, 32 NZD concession; season and multi-day passes are better value if you stay. You can pedal everything, or take a van shuttle to the lower mountain or a Can-Am buggy boost to the summit - shuttles need booking 48 hours ahead and run only when conditions allow.

    Open season
Open all year (trail conditions and shuttles vary with the weather).
Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Wanaka | Car | ~15 min
Queenstown | Car | ~1h15

    Source: Bike Glendhu.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.758470" lon="146.966060">
    <name>Mystic Bike Park - Bright (Victoria, AU) [100 AUD]</name>
    <desc>Mystic Hill 790 m - the top shuttle drop-off

    Trails
Over 60 km of trail across 20-plus tracks on the hill directly above Bright, and the centre of gravity riding in the Victorian High Country. Everything from technical natural singletrack to fast gravity flow and big jump lines, with the network dropping around 460 m to town. Bright itself is a genuine mountain-bike town, which makes this an easy place to spend a week.

    Getting up / price
Elevation Mystic runs the uplift: a one-day Gravity Pass is 100 AUD for unlimited shuttles to several drop zones, and every rider also needs a Mountain Pass (1-day, 7-day or annual) on top. Book ahead - it sells out even off-peak, and walk-ins pay a 5 AUD surcharge.

    Open season
Open all year. Uplift 09:30-16:00 in autumn, winter and spring; 08:00-14:30 in summer to dodge the heat.
Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:00
Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Melbourne | Car | ~3h30
Albury | Car | ~1h30

    Source: Elevation Mystic.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-36.741880" lon="146.976140">
    <name>Mystic Bike Park: trailhead</name>
    <desc>Mystic Park trailhead at 330 m on the edge of Bright - shuttle pick-up, parking and the end of every descent.</desc>
