  <wpt lat="41.781290" lon="23.439490">
    <name>Bansko Bike Park (Pirin Mountains) [40 EUR]</name>
    <desc>Banderishka Polyana 1600 m - top of the Bansko gondola

    Trails
Bulgaria's largest commercial bike park, on the north side of Pirin National Park. The mapped OSM lines around Banderishka Polyana are unnamed in OpenStreetMap but cover a mix of downhill/enduro terrain: roughly grade 2 (intermediate flow), grade 3 (advanced/rough), and grade 4 (expert). The resort also publishes guided e-bike/enduro tours in the wider Pirin area (Vihren hut, Banya, Dobrinishte, Dancing Bears Park). Trail signage on the ground should be followed; OSM lines are indicative only.

    Getting up / price
Main uplift is the Bansko gondola from the village to Banderishka Polyana. The downhill day pass (covers gondola + bike transport) is 40 EUR adult / 38 EUR students and retirees / 32 EUR child 7-11. A one-way gondola ticket with bicycle is 30 EUR adult. Banderitsa 1 and 2 chairlifts can be used for higher laps with a separate one-way ticket (24 EUR adult) and run by advance request for groups over 40.

    Open season
Open from 27 June; closed from 7 September (published 2026 dates: 27 June - 6 September inclusive).
Daily opening hours: gondola 08:30-17:00; chairlifts 08:45-16:15
Operator reserves the right to adjust dates and prices.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Sofia | Car / bus | ~2h15 (150 km)
Thessaloniki | Car | ~3h (220 km)
Istanbul | Car | ~6-7h (600 km)

    Sources: Banskoski summer attractions and prices and Banskoski lifts and slopes.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
