  <wpt lat="42.554610" lon="1.653710">
    <name>Grandvalira Bike Park / E-Bike Trails - Soldeu / El Tarter (Andorra) [23 EUR]</name>
    <desc>TSD6 Solana top 2470 m - highest lift-served start in the Soldeu / El Tarter sector

    Trails
Lift-served riding in the Soldeu / El Tarter sector of Grandvalira. The area historically offered downhill, freeride, enduro, cross-country and rally lines. In 2026 the official summer product is the Grandvalira E-Bike Trails network (111 km), with the Bike Pass giving up to four lift ascents per day on the Soldeu, Canillo and Funicamp sectors. A small number of OSM-recorded mtb:scale descents remain in the sector.

    Getting up / price
The Bike Pass uses the TC8 Soldeu gondola from Soldeu village and the TSD6 Solana chair to reach the highest freeride start points. 2026 Bike Pass: EUR 23 for ages 6-74 (4 lift ascents per day between Encamp/Funicamp, Canillo and Soldeu); under-5 and 75+ free; optional insurance EUR 12.

    Open season
Open from 21 June; closed from 27 September (Grandvalira 2026 summer season; individual lifts have shorter calendars, e.g. Funicamp from 11 July to 8 September).
Daily opening hours: check sector-specific schedules.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Andorra la Vella | Bus / car | ~20 min
Barcelona Airport | Car / bus | ~3h

    Sources: Grandvalira E-Bike Trails, summer opening hours,
    legacy Soldeu Bike Park info from Andorramania, and MoreDirt.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</desc>
  </wpt>
