  <wpt lat="46.255570" lon="7.923030">
    <name>Visperterminen / Giw [chairlift fare]</name>
    <desc>Giw 1955 m - top of the Sesselbahn Visperterminen-Giw chairlift

    Trails
Visperterminen in the Valais Alps offers lift-served mountain biking via the Giw chairlift, featuring the famous Giw Enduro trail dropping 1,300 vertical metres down to Visp. The area delivers fast descents, technical singletracks, and panoramic alpine loops from the Giw ridge.

- Giw Enduro (Route 548): 12.4 km from Giw to Visp, over 1,300 m drop. Sustained enduro on open alpine terrain, forest singletrack and steep switchbacks.

    - Heida Bike-Loop (Route 547): Exposed scenic all-mountain tour with regional viewpoints above the Rhone valley.
- Parmili Trail: Technical and fun singletrack toward Visp.
- Phoenix aus der Asche: 9.5 km descent from Visperterminen to Visp, 800 m drop.

    Getting up / price
Chairlift from Visperterminen (1379 m) to Giw (1955 m). Confirm price locally.

    Open season
Open from June; closed from October.
Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00
Typical summer estimate; confirm chairlift schedule.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Visp | Car / bus | ~15 min
Brig | Train + bus | ~25 min
Sion | Car | ~45 min

    Sources: Visperterminen tourism and SwissMobility Route 548.</desc>
  </wpt>
