  <wpt lat="45.605890" lon="-63.547390">
    <name>Wentworth Bike Park (Nova Scotia, Canada) [chairlift]</name>
    <desc>Blue Quad top station 283 m - Nova Scotia's only lift-accessible bike park

    Trails
More than 40 km of gravity riding is split between the chairlift-served Lift Zone and the pedal-access Climb Zone. The network includes progressive flow, jumps and technical downhill trails, plus cross-country riding near the summit. Rentals, lessons and a downhill race series are available.

    Getting up / price
The Blue Quad serves the Lift Zone. Published 2026 adult day tickets are CAD 55 in advance or CAD 60 on the day; separate lower-cost Climb Zone access is available.

    Open season
Tentative 2026 lift season: 13 June through late October, Friday-Sunday and selected holidays.
Weather and trail work can change lift and trail availability; check the live status before travelling.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Truro | Car | ~35 min
Halifax | Car | ~1h45

    Sources: official Bike Wentworth, 2026 Lift Zone information, 2026 tickets and OSM Blue Quad lift (ODbL). Pin marks the OSM lift top, verified at 283 m.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.538780" lon="-62.113390">
    <name>Keppoch Mountain (Nova Scotia, Canada) [shuttle]</name>
    <desc>Weekend shuttle drop-off around 218 m above Antigonish

    Trails
Almost 30 km of purpose-built mountain-bike trails range from beginner flow to expert natural and technical descents. The community-operated park also has a skills area, bike wash and repair station, and hosts downhill and enduro events.

    Getting up / price
Weekend bike shuttles carry riders to the upper trail network; pedal access is also possible. Buy a day or season pass through Keppoch and check capacity before travelling.

    Open season
Published 2026 shuttle opening: 23 May. Standard service runs Saturday-Sunday, 10:00-17:00, generally through late October.
Potential Friday evening services are announced separately.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Antigonish | Car | ~15 min
Halifax | Car | ~2h

    Sources: official 2026 shuttle opening and Tourism Nova Scotia park information. Pin marks the upper Summit West trailhead, elevation-checked at 218 m.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.976650" lon="-66.687140">
    <name>Sugarloaf Bike Park (New Brunswick, Canada) [chairlift]</name>
    <desc>Chairlift top station 195 m - Atlantic Canada's original lift-access bike park

    Trails
About 49 km of riding and 36 listed trails combine Gravity Logic-built flow, jump lines, drops and wooden features with rocky expert downhill and year-round cross-country trails. The lower mountain includes a family skills park and pump track.

    Getting up / price
The chairlift serves the downhill network. Published 2026 full-day tickets are CAD 47.52 adult and CAD 39.60 youth/student/senior; rentals and one-ride tickets are available.

    Open season
Published 2026 bike-park season: 30 May-27 September. Weekends in spring and fall; Thursday-Sunday from late June through early September.
Typical hours: 10:00-19:30 Thursday-Saturday and 10:00-16:30 Sunday in high summer.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Campbellton | Car / bike | ~10 min
Bathurst | Car | ~1h

    Sources: official bike-park overview and trail totals, 2026 tickets and schedule and the OSM-mapped chairlift (ODbL). Pin marks its upper endpoint, verified at 195 m.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.675925" lon="-65.376522">
    <name>Poley Mountain Bike Park (New Brunswick, Canada) [chairlift]</name>
    <desc>Quad Chair top station 278 m - lift-served riding in the Waterford hills

    Trails
A compact gravity park with beginner-friendly flow, natural intermediate and expert descents, jumps and technical forest sections. Riders can combine the lift-served network with pedal-access multi-use trails; bike rentals are available.

    Getting up / price
The Quad Chair carries bikes. Poley sells day access and 2026 summer passes with or without chairlift access; the published adult lift-included season pass is CAD 300.

    Open season
Published 2026 summer bike season runs June-October, with regular Friday-Sunday operations.
Daily hours, lift choice and trail status vary; consult the current report before travelling.

    Access
From | Transport | Duration
Sussex | Car | ~15 min
Saint John / Moncton | Car | ~1h

    Sources: official 2026 summer bike information and OSM Quad Chair way 257027285 (ODbL). Pin marks the upper lift endpoint, verified at 278 m.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.336900" lon="16.395700">
    <name>Family Bike Park Zieleniec (PL) [cable car]</name>
    <desc>Gryglowka and Nartorama - nearly 10 km of lift-served trails

Five signed routes range from gentle beginner flow to the steep natural Crazy Dad line. Cable cars carry bikes to the route starts; rentals and instruction are available.

Source: official Family Bike Park Zieleniec.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.365800" lon="20.755500">
    <name>Wierchomla Bike Park (PL) [chairlift]</name>
    <desc>Dwie Doliny Wierchomla Mala - lift-served downhill and enduro

A Beskid gravity park with marked downhill and freeride lines, plus pedal-access forest routes. Expect natural roots and rocks between shaped sections.

Sources: Poland Travel park profile and Wierchomla resort.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.443500" lon="20.300900">
    <name>Bike Park Kluszkowce (PL) [chairlift]</name>
    <desc>Wdjar mountain above Kluszkowce - compact gravity riding

A purpose-built park on the Wdjar ski slope with downhill, flow and jump lines including the A-line. The chairlift serves bike routes during summer operations.

Source: Czorsztyn municipality and resort information; confirm current schedules locally.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="29.961500" lon="31.340500">
    <name>Wadi Degla Protectorate MTB (Egypt) [no lift]</name>
    <desc>Desert valley trail network on Cairo's southeastern edge

Wadi Degla is a protected 30 km limestone valley with rocky and sandy tracks used by Cairo mountain bikers. This is natural cross-country and all-mountain riding, not a formal lift park.

Sources: Cairo Governorate reserve information and local MTB route documentation.</desc>
  </wpt>
  <trk>
    <name>Weissenstein: Flowtrail</name>
    <desc>1.8 km marked flow trail

Built MTB flow trail descending from the Weissenstein gondola area toward Oberdorf, with berms, rollers and intermediate features.

Geometry simplified from OpenStreetMap way 1148325073 (ODbL). Trail description and lift context: Seilbahn Weissenstein. Indicative line; follow local signs and conditions.</desc>
